window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/a442-3eeab048859d2373.json"]={sha256:"3eeab048859d23731eb33e9ed386fae62f8d59a12064edc92060bc657e2defe3",value:{"id":"a442","title":"穿透電子顯微鏡","titleEn":"Transmission electron microscopes","category":"instruments","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以 300 kV 穿透電子顯微鏡為對象：從 1.97 pm 的電子波長與布拉格繞射出發，推導 Scherzer 解析度、對比傳遞函數與色像差資訊極限，理解六極 Cs 校正器為何把解析度推到 0.1 nm 以下，再把高壓與透鏡電流的 ppm 級穩定度、樣品厚度與撞擊損傷、場址環境與驗收測試整合成可交付的工程紀錄。","summaryEn":"Taking a 300 kV transmission electron microscope: start from the 1.97 pm electron wavelength and Bragg diffraction, derive Scherzer resolution, the contrast transfer function and the chromatic information limit, see why a hexapole Cs corrector pushes resolution below 0.1 nm, then integrate ppm-level high-voltage and lens-current stability, specimen thickness and knock-on damage, site environment and acceptance tests into a deliverable engineering record.","scope":"依公開物理原理與官方資料編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是原廠配方、施工圖、設備操作許可或安全程序。數值均為教學假設，需依實際規格重算。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public physics and official sources. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, operating authorisation or safety procedures. Numbers are teaching assumptions and must be recalculated for real specifications.","subcategory":"optics-analytical-instruments","subcategoryTitle":"電子、離子與分析儀器","subcategoryTitleEn":"Electron, ion and analytical instruments","learningTrack":"optics","learningSubdiscipline":"optics-analytical-instruments","learningTags":["optics","optics-analytical-instruments","electron"],"architectureFamily":"electron","architectureNodes":[["Schottky 槍與 300 kV 高壓槽","Schottky gun and 300 kV high-voltage tank"],["聚光鏡與單色器","Condenser lenses and monochromator"],["物鏡極靴與樣品載台","Objective pole piece and specimen holder"],["六極 Cs 校正器","Hexapole Cs corrector"],["投影鏡與直接電子偵測器","Projector lenses and direct electron detector"],["EELS 能量過濾器","EELS energy filter"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5]],"diagram":{"type":"electron","labels":["Schottky 槍與 300 kV 高壓槽","聚光鏡與單色器","物鏡極靴與樣品載台","六極 Cs 校正器","投影鏡與直接電子偵測器"],"labelsEn":["Schottky gun and 300 kV high-voltage tank","Condenser lenses and monochromator","Objective pole piece and specimen holder","Hexapole Cs corrector","Projector lenses and direct electron detector"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"300 kV 解析度預算練習：λ = 1.97 pm。未校正、C_s = 0.6 mm：Scherzer 解析度 d_S = 0.66×(0.6×10⁻³×(1.97×10⁻¹²)³)^¼ ≈ 0.17 nm，Scherzer 離焦 −1.2×√(0.6×10⁻³×1.97×10⁻¹²) ≈ −41 nm，最佳光圈半角 (4λ/C_s)^¼ ≈ 10.7 mrad；矽 [110] 的 0.136 nm 啞鈴無法分開。裝上六極校正器把 C_s 壓到 µm 等級後，光圈由 C₅ = 5 mm 限制在 (λ/C₅)^⅙ ≈ 27 mrad，解析度改由資訊極限決定：C_c = 1.4 mm、Schottky ΔE = 0.7 eV、ΔV/V = 1 ppm、ΔI/I = 0.5 ppm 給焦距散佈 Δ ≈ 4.5 nm、d_info = √(πλΔ/2) ≈ 0.12 nm，啞鈴勉強可分；加單色器到 ΔE = 0.2 eV 後 Δ ≈ 2.3 nm、d_info ≈ 0.084 nm，啞鈴清楚分開。若樣品是石墨烯，300 kV 的最大傳遞能量 71 eV 遠超 17 eV 的位移閾值，必須降到 80 kV（15.8 eV），此時 λ = 4.18 pm，同樣的 Δ 給 d_info ≈ 0.12 nm，仍足以分辨 0.213 nm 的碳六員環間距。數值為教學假設，不代表任何儀器規格。","textEn":"300 kV resolution-budget exercise: λ = 1.97 pm. Uncorrected with C_s = 0.6 mm: Scherzer resolution d_S = 0.66×(0.6×10⁻³×(1.97×10⁻¹²)³)^¼ ≈ 0.17 nm, Scherzer defocus −1.2×√(0.6×10⁻³×1.97×10⁻¹²) ≈ −41 nm, optimum semi-angle (4λ/C_s)^¼ ≈ 10.7 mrad; the 0.136 nm silicon [110] dumbbells cannot be separated. With a hexapole corrector bringing C_s to the micrometre level, the aperture is limited by C₅ = 5 mm at (λ/C₅)^⅙ ≈ 27 mrad and resolution passes to the information limit: C_c = 1.4 mm, Schottky ΔE = 0.7 eV, ΔV/V = 1 ppm and ΔI/I = 0.5 ppm give a focal spread Δ ≈ 4.5 nm and d_info = √(πλΔ/2) ≈ 0.12 nm, barely resolving the dumbbells; a monochromator at ΔE = 0.2 eV gives Δ ≈ 2.3 nm and d_info ≈ 0.084 nm, resolving them clearly. For graphene the 71 eV maximum transfer at 300 kV far exceeds the 17 eV displacement threshold, so the voltage must drop to 80 kV (15.8 eV), where λ = 4.18 pm and the same Δ gives d_info ≈ 0.12 nm, still enough for the 0.213 nm carbon-ring spacing. Values are teaching assumptions, not any instrument's specification.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變系統邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not measured hardware, product ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after changing the system boundary.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與設施背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and facility context, not these numbers."},"depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":12,"enrichmentVersion":12,"stages":[{"id":"a442-v12-s1","title":"系統邊界與物理原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and physical principles","description":"本階段聚焦「電子波長、散射與對比機制」與「相位對比傳遞、Scherzer 解析度與 Cs 校正」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Electron wavelength, scattering and contrast mechanisms\" and \"Phase-contrast transfer, Scherzer resolution and Cs correction\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a442-v12-01","title":"電子波長、散射與對比機制：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Electron wavelength, scattering and contrast mechanisms: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「薄樣品、繞射與影像平面」如何決定穿透電子顯微鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thin specimen, diffraction and image planes” determines the key performance of “Transmission electron microscopes”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"穿透電子顯微鏡讓高能電子穿過厚度數十奈米的薄樣品，物鏡把透射與散射電子在後焦面形成繞射圖、在像平面形成影像，後續的中間鏡與投影鏡選擇放大哪一個平面。對比有三種來源：質量厚度對比來自被物鏡光圈擋掉的高角散射；繞射對比來自晶體特定取向滿足布拉格條件；相位對比來自透射束與繞射束在像平面的干涉，是晶格影像的基礎。300 kV 的電子波長只有 1.97 pm，布拉格角只有幾個毫弧度，所以整個光學系統在極小角度內工作，像差成為主要限制。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「薄樣品、繞射與影像平面」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A transmission electron microscope sends high-energy electrons through a specimen tens of nanometres thick; the objective lens forms a diffraction pattern in its back focal plane and an image in the image plane, and intermediate and projector lenses choose which plane to magnify. Contrast has three origins: mass-thickness contrast from high-angle scattering stopped by the objective aperture; diffraction contrast from crystal orientations satisfying Bragg's condition; and phase contrast from interference of transmitted and diffracted beams in the image plane, the basis of lattice imaging. At 300 kV the electron wavelength is only 1.97 pm and Bragg angles are a few milliradians, so the whole optical system works within tiny angles and aberrations become the dominant limit. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Thin specimen, diffraction and image planes”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：相對論波長 λ = h/√(2m₀eV(1 + eV/2m₀c²))：80 kV 4.18 pm、200 kV 2.51 pm、300 kV 1.97 pm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Relativistic wavelength λ = h/√(2m₀eV(1 + eV/2m₀c²)): 4.18 pm at 80 kV, 2.51 pm at 200 kV, 1.97 pm at 300 kV.","failure":"常見誤解：「穿透電子顯微鏡的影像對比和光學顯微鏡一樣來自吸收。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"TEM image contrast comes from absorption, as in a light microscope.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「薄樣品、繞射與影像平面」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Thin specimen, diffraction and image planes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-01-k1","title":"電子波長、散射與對比機制","titleEn":"Electron wavelength, scattering and contrast mechanisms","text":"穿透電子顯微鏡讓高能電子穿過厚度數十奈米的薄樣品，物鏡把透射與散射電子在後焦面形成繞射圖、在像平面形成影像，後續的中間鏡與投影鏡選擇放大哪一個平面。對比有三種來源：質量厚度對比來自被物鏡光圈擋掉的高角散射；繞射對比來自晶體特定取向滿足布拉格條件；相位對比來自透射束與繞射束在像平面的干涉，是晶格影像的基礎。","textEn":"A transmission electron microscope sends high-energy electrons through a specimen tens of nanometres thick; the objective lens forms a diffraction pattern in its back focal plane and an image in the image plane, and intermediate and projector lenses choose which plane to magnify. Contrast has three origins: mass-thickness contrast from high-angle scattering stopped by the objective aperture; diffraction contrast from crystal orientations satisfying Bragg's condition; and phase contrast from interference of transmitted and diffracted beams in the image plane, the basis of lattice imaging.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：穿透電子顯微鏡的影像對比和光學顯微鏡一樣來自吸收。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: TEM image contrast comes from absorption, as in a light microscope. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電子波長、散射與對比機制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Electron wavelength, scattering and contrast mechanisms\" is correct?","options":["穿透電子顯微鏡的影像對比和光學顯微鏡一樣來自吸收。","穿透電子顯微鏡讓高能電子穿過厚度數十奈米的薄樣品，物鏡把透射與散射電子在後焦面形成繞射圖、在像平面形成影像，後續的中間鏡與投影鏡選擇放大哪一個平面。","Cs 校正後解析度只受電子波長限制，可以達到皮米。"],"optionsEn":["TEM image contrast comes from absorption, as in a light microscope.","A transmission electron microscope sends high-energy electrons through a specimen tens of nanometres thick.","After Cs correction resolution is limited only by electron wavelength and reaches picometres."],"answer":1,"explanation":"穿透電子顯微鏡讓高能電子穿過厚度數十奈米的薄樣品，物鏡把透射與散射電子在後焦面形成繞射圖、在像平面形成影像，後續的中間鏡與投影鏡選擇放大哪一個平面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A transmission electron microscope sends high-energy electrons through a specimen tens of nanometres thick; the objective lens forms a diffraction pattern in its back focal plane and an image in the image plane, and intermediate and projector lenses choose which plane to magnify. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"a442-v12-02","title":"電子波長、散射與對比機制：定量估算","titleEn":"Electron wavelength, scattering and contrast mechanisms: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「薄樣品、繞射與影像平面」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thin specimen, diffraction and image planes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：相對論波長 λ = h/√(2m₀eV(1 + eV/2m₀c²))：80 kV 4.18 pm、200 kV 2.51 pm、300 kV 1.97 pm。布拉格角 θ_B ≈ λ/(2d)：矽 (111) d = 0.3136 nm 在 300 kV 為 3.14 mrad = 0.18°；矽 [110] 啞鈴間距 0.136 nm 對應 7.2 mrad。繞射圖中環的半徑 R = L·λ/d：相機長度 L = 0.5 m、金 (111) d = 0.2355 nm 時 R = 4.18 mm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Relativistic wavelength λ = h/√(2m₀eV(1 + eV/2m₀c²)): 4.18 pm at 80 kV, 2.51 pm at 200 kV, 1.97 pm at 300 kV. Bragg angle θ_B ≈ λ/(2d): silicon (111) with d = 0.3136 nm gives 3.14 mrad = 0.18° at 300 kV; the 0.136 nm silicon [110] dumbbell spacing corresponds to 7.2 mrad. Ring radius in the diffraction pattern R = L·λ/d: at camera length L = 0.5 m and gold (111) d = 0.2355 nm, R = 4.18 mm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以多晶金薄膜拍選區繞射圖，量 (111)、(200)、(220) 環半徑，與 R = Lλ/d 計算值比較以校正相機長度；再把矽單晶轉到 [110] 帶軸，確認繞射點的角度分佈與計算的布拉格角一致，並切換物鏡光圈大小觀察質量厚度與繞射對比的消長。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record a selected-area diffraction pattern of polycrystalline gold, measure the (111), (200) and (220) ring radii and compare with R = Lλ/d to calibrate camera length; tilt a silicon crystal to the [110] zone axis, confirm the angular distribution of spots matches the computed Bragg angles, and change the objective aperture size to watch mass-thickness and diffraction contrast trade off.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"相對論波長 λ = h/√(2m₀eV(1 + eV/2m₀c²))：80 kV 4.18 pm、200 kV 2.51 pm、300 kV 1.97 pm。布拉格角 θ_B ≈ λ/(2d)：矽 (111) d = 0.3136 nm 在 300 kV 為 3.14 mrad = 0.18°；矽 [110] 啞鈴間距 0.136 nm 對應 7.2 mrad。繞射圖中環的半徑 R = L·λ/d：相機長度 L = 0.5 m、金 (111) d = 0.2355 nm 時 R = 4.18 mm。","textEn":"Relativistic wavelength λ = h/√(2m₀eV(1 + eV/2m₀c²)): 4.18 pm at 80 kV, 2.51 pm at 200 kV, 1.97 pm at 300 kV. Bragg angle θ_B ≈ λ/(2d): silicon (111) with d = 0.3136 nm gives 3.14 mrad = 0.18° at 300 kV; the 0.136 nm silicon [110] dumbbell spacing corresponds to 7.2 mrad. Ring radius in the diffraction pattern R = L·λ/d: at camera length L = 0.5 m and gold (111) d = 0.2355 nm, R = 4.18 mm.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「電子波長、散射與對比機制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Electron wavelength, scattering and contrast mechanisms\", which statement holds?","options":["極靴間隙越小越好，因為像差係數更低。","加速電壓越高穿透力越強，所以總是對樣品更溫和。","相對論波長 λ = h/√(2m₀eV(1 + eV/2m₀c²))：80 kV 4.18 pm、200 kV 2.51 pm、300 kV 1.97 pm。"],"optionsEn":["A smaller pole-piece gap is always better because aberration coefficients are lower.","Higher accelerating voltage penetrates better and is therefore always gentler on the specimen.","Relativistic wavelength λ = h/√(2m₀eV(1 + eV/2m₀c²)): 4.18 pm at 80 kV, 2.51 pm at 200 kV, 1.97 pm at 300 kV."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相對論波長 λ = h/√(2m₀eV(1 + eV/2m₀c²))：80 kV 4.18 pm、200 kV 2.51 pm、300 kV 1.97 pm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Relativistic wavelength λ = h/√(2m₀eV(1 + eV/2m₀c²)): 4.18 pm at 80 kV, 2.51 pm at 200 kV, 1.97 pm at 300 kV. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"a442-v12-03","title":"電子波長、散射與對比機制：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Electron wavelength, scattering and contrast mechanisms: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「薄樣品、繞射與影像平面」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Thin specimen, diffraction and image planes” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以多晶金薄膜拍選區繞射圖，量 (111)、(200)、(220) 環半徑，與 R = Lλ/d 計算值比較以校正相機長度；再把矽單晶轉到 [110] 帶軸，確認繞射點的角度分佈與計算的布拉格角一致，並切換物鏡光圈大小觀察質量厚度與繞射對比的消長。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record a selected-area diffraction pattern of polycrystalline gold, measure the (111), (200) and (220) ring radii and compare with R = Lλ/d to calibrate camera length; tilt a silicon crystal to the [110] zone axis, confirm the angular distribution of spots matches the computed Bragg angles, and change the objective aperture size to watch mass-thickness and diffraction contrast trade off. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：樣品厚度超過 100 nm 時多重散射與非彈性散射主導，晶格影像的相位對比消失、繞射點被動力學效應改寫，分析者用運動學公式解讀點強度而得到錯誤的結構結論。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A specimen thicker than 100 nm is dominated by multiple and inelastic scattering, lattice phase contrast vanishes and spot intensities are rewritten by dynamical effects; interpreting them with kinematic formulas yields wrong structural conclusions.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多晶金薄膜拍選區繞射圖，量 (111)、(200)、(220) 環半徑，與 R = Lλ/d 計算值比較以校正相機長度；再把矽單晶轉到 [110] 帶軸，確認繞射點的角度分佈與計算的布拉格角一致，並切換物鏡光圈大小觀察質量厚度與繞射對比的消長。","textEn":"Record a selected-area diffraction pattern of polycrystalline gold, measure the (111), (200) and (220) ring radii and compare with R = Lλ/d to calibrate camera length; tilt a silicon crystal to the [110] zone axis, confirm the angular distribution of spots matches the computed Bragg angles, and change the objective aperture size to watch mass-thickness and diffraction contrast trade off.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-03-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「電子波長、散射與對比機制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Electron wavelength, scattering and contrast mechanisms\"?","options":["以多晶金薄膜拍選區繞射圖，量 (111)、(200)、(220) 環半徑，與 R = Lλ/d 計算值比較以校正相機長度。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","顯微鏡放在地下室就自動滿足振動與磁場規格。"],"optionsEn":["Record a selected-area diffraction pattern of polycrystalline gold, measure the (111), (200) and (220) ring radii and compare with R = Lλ/d to calibrate camera length.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Putting the microscope in a basement automatically satisfies vibration and field specifications."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以多晶金薄膜拍選區繞射圖，量 (111)、(200)、(220) 環半徑，與 R = Lλ/d 計算值比較以校正相機長度；再把矽單晶轉到 [110] 帶軸，確認繞射點的角度分佈與計算的布拉格角一致，並切換物鏡光圈大小觀察質量厚度與繞射對比的消長。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record a selected-area diffraction pattern of polycrystalline gold, measure the (111), (200) and (220) ring radii and compare with R = Lλ/d to calibrate camera length; tilt a silicon crystal to the [110] zone axis, confirm the angular distribution of spots matches the computed Bragg angles, and change the objective aperture size to watch mass-thickness and diffraction contrast trade off. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"a442-v12-04","title":"電子波長、散射與對比機制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Electron wavelength, scattering and contrast mechanisms: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「薄樣品、繞射與影像平面」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Thin specimen, diffraction and image planes” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"樣品厚度超過 100 nm 時多重散射與非彈性散射主導，晶格影像的相位對比消失、繞射點被動力學效應改寫，分析者用運動學公式解讀點強度而得到錯誤的結構結論。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A specimen thicker than 100 nm is dominated by multiple and inelastic scattering, lattice phase contrast vanishes and spot intensities are rewritten by dynamical effects; interpreting them with kinematic formulas yields wrong structural conclusions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：300 kV 的電子波長只有 1.97 pm，布拉格角只有幾個毫弧度，所以整個光學系統在極小角度內工作，像差成為主要限制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: At 300 kV the electron wavelength is only 1.97 pm and Bragg angles are a few milliradians, so the whole optical system works within tiny angles and aberrations become the dominant limit.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「穿透電子顯微鏡的影像對比和光學顯微鏡一樣來自吸收。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"TEM image contrast comes from absorption, as in a light microscope.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"樣品厚度超過 100 nm 時多重散射與非彈性散射主導，晶格影像的相位對比消失、繞射點被動力學效應改寫，分析者用運動學公式解讀點強度而得到錯誤的結構結論。","textEn":"A specimen thicker than 100 nm is dominated by multiple and inelastic scattering, lattice phase contrast vanishes and spot intensities are rewritten by dynamical effects; interpreting them with kinematic formulas yields wrong structural conclusions.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電子波長、散射與對比機制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Electron wavelength, scattering and contrast mechanisms\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","樣品厚度超過 100 nm 時多重散射與非彈性散射主導，晶格影像的相位對比消失、繞射點被動力學效應改寫，分析者用運動學公式解讀點強度而得到錯誤的結構結論。","Cs 校正後解析度只受電子波長限制，可以達到皮米。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","A specimen thicker than 100 nm is dominated by multiple and inelastic scattering, lattice phase contrast vanishes and spot intensities are rewritten by dynamical effects.","After Cs correction resolution is limited only by electron wavelength and reaches picometres."],"answer":1,"explanation":"樣品厚度超過 100 nm 時多重散射與非彈性散射主導，晶格影像的相位對比消失、繞射點被動力學效應改寫，分析者用運動學公式解讀點強度而得到錯誤的結構結論。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A specimen thicker than 100 nm is dominated by multiple and inelastic scattering, lattice phase contrast vanishes and spot intensities are rewritten by dynamical effects; interpreting them with kinematic formulas yields wrong structural conclusions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"a442-v12-05","title":"相位對比傳遞、Scherzer 解析度與 Cs 校正：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Phase-contrast transfer, Scherzer resolution and Cs correction: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-04"],"objective":"說明「對比傳遞函數與 Scherzer 離焦」如何決定穿透電子顯微鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Contrast transfer function and Scherzer defocus” determines the key performance of “Transmission electron microscopes”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"薄樣品是弱相位物體，影像對比由對比傳遞函數 CTF(u) = sin χ(u) 決定，χ(u) = πλΔf·u² + (π/2)·C_s·λ³·u⁴，u 是空間頻率。球面像差 C_s 讓相位隨 u⁴ 快速振盪，CTF 在第一個過零點之後正負交替，影像不再直觀；Scherzer 離焦把 Δf 選成讓低頻段形成最寬的負值通帶，第一個過零點定義點解析度。六極或八極 Cs 校正器產生負的球面像差抵銷物鏡的正值，使 C_s 可調到接近零甚至微負，過零點外推到色像差資訊極限，解析度由 0.17 nm 進入 0.1 nm 以下，並消除離域效應。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「對比傳遞函數與 Scherzer 離焦」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A thin specimen is a weak phase object whose image contrast follows the contrast transfer function CTF(u) = sin χ(u) with χ(u) = πλΔf·u² + (π/2)·C_s·λ³·u⁴ and u the spatial frequency. Spherical aberration C_s makes the phase oscillate rapidly with u⁴, so beyond the first zero the CTF alternates sign and the image stops being intuitive; Scherzer defocus chooses Δf to form the widest negative passband at low frequency, and the first zero defines point resolution. A hexapole or octupole Cs corrector produces negative spherical aberration to cancel the objective's positive value, letting C_s be tuned near zero or slightly negative, pushing the first zero out to the chromatic information limit, taking resolution from 0.17 nm to below 0.1 nm and removing delocalisation. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Contrast transfer function and Scherzer defocus”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Scherzer 點解析度 d_S = 0.66·(C_s·λ³)^¼，Scherzer 離焦 Δf_S = −1.2·√(C_s·λ)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Scherzer point resolution d_S = 0.66·(C_s·λ³)^¼ and Scherzer defocus Δf_S = −1.2·√(C_s·λ).","failure":"常見誤解：「Cs 校正後解析度只受電子波長限制，可以達到皮米。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"After Cs correction resolution is limited only by electron wavelength and reaches picometres.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「對比傳遞函數與 Scherzer 離焦」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Contrast transfer function and Scherzer defocus”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-05-k1","title":"相位對比傳遞、Scherzer 解析度與 Cs 校正","titleEn":"Phase-contrast transfer, Scherzer resolution and Cs correction","text":"薄樣品是弱相位物體，影像對比由對比傳遞函數 CTF(u) = sin χ(u) 決定，χ(u) = πλΔf·u² + (π/2)·C_s·λ³·u⁴，u 是空間頻率。球面像差 C_s 讓相位隨 u⁴ 快速振盪，CTF 在第一個過零點之後正負交替，影像不再直觀；Scherzer 離焦把 Δf 選成讓低頻段形成最寬的負值通帶，第一個過零點定義點解析度。","textEn":"A thin specimen is a weak phase object whose image contrast follows the contrast transfer function CTF(u) = sin χ(u) with χ(u) = πλΔf·u² + (π/2)·C_s·λ³·u⁴ and u the spatial frequency. Spherical aberration C_s makes the phase oscillate rapidly with u⁴, so beyond the first zero the CTF alternates sign and the image stops being intuitive; Scherzer defocus chooses Δf to form the widest negative passband at low frequency, and the first zero defines point resolution.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：Cs 校正後解析度只受電子波長限制，可以達到皮米。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: After Cs correction resolution is limited only by electron wavelength and reaches picometres. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「相位對比傳遞、Scherzer 解析度與 Cs 校正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Phase-contrast transfer, Scherzer resolution and Cs correction\" is correct?","options":["Cs 校正後解析度只受電子波長限制，可以達到皮米。","只要像差校正器調好，電子槍的能量散佈就無關緊要。","薄樣品是弱相位物體，影像對比由對比傳遞函數 CTF(u) = sin χ(u) 決定，χ(u) = πλΔf·u² + (π/2)·C_s·λ³·u⁴，u 是空間頻率。"],"optionsEn":["After Cs correction resolution is limited only by electron wavelength and reaches picometres.","Once the corrector is tuned, the gun's energy spread no longer matters.","A thin specimen is a weak phase object whose image contrast follows the contrast transfer function CTF(u) = sin χ(u) with χ(u) = πλΔf·u² + (π/2)·C_s·λ³·u⁴ and u the spatial frequency."],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄樣品是弱相位物體，影像對比由對比傳遞函數 CTF(u) = sin χ(u) 決定，χ(u) = πλΔf·u² + (π/2)·C_s·λ³·u⁴，u 是空間頻率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A thin specimen is a weak phase object whose image contrast follows the contrast transfer function CTF(u) = sin χ(u) with χ(u) = πλΔf·u² + (π/2)·C_s·λ³·u⁴ and u the spatial frequency. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"a442-v12-06","title":"相位對比傳遞、Scherzer 解析度與 Cs 校正：定量估算","titleEn":"Phase-contrast transfer, Scherzer resolution and Cs correction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「對比傳遞函數與 Scherzer 離焦」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Contrast transfer function and Scherzer defocus” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Scherzer 點解析度 d_S = 0.66·(C_s·λ³)^¼，Scherzer 離焦 Δf_S = −1.2·√(C_s·λ)。300 kV、λ = 1.97 pm：C_s = 0.6 mm 給 d_S = 0.17 nm、Δf_S = −41 nm；C_s = 1.2 mm 給 0.20 nm、−58 nm。最佳物鏡光圈半角 α ≈ (4λ/C_s)^¼ ≈ 10.7 mrad。校正器把 C_s 壓到 µm 等級後，光圈由五階像差 C₅ 限制，C₅ = 5 mm 時 α ≈ (λ/C₅)^⅙ ≈ 27 mrad，可接受的角度大了 2.5 倍，解析度改由資訊極限決定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Scherzer point resolution d_S = 0.66·(C_s·λ³)^¼ and Scherzer defocus Δf_S = −1.2·√(C_s·λ). At 300 kV with λ = 1.97 pm: C_s = 0.6 mm gives d_S = 0.17 nm and Δf_S = −41 nm; C_s = 1.2 mm gives 0.20 nm and −58 nm. The optimum objective semi-angle is α ≈ (4λ/C_s)^¼ ≈ 10.7 mrad. Once a corrector brings C_s to the micrometre level the aperture is limited by fifth-order aberration C₅: with C₅ = 5 mm, α ≈ (λ/C₅)^⅙ ≈ 27 mrad, 2.5 times the accepted angle, and resolution passes to the information limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：在非晶碳膜上拍一系列離焦影像並對每張做傅立葉轉換，Thon 環的半徑序列給出 CTF 的過零點，擬合 χ(u) 可同時解出 Δf 與 C_s；用 Zemlin 離焦傾斜表（在不同束傾角下的 Thon 環）量 C_s、彗差與三重像散；校正後重拍，確認第一過零點移到 0.1 nm 以外且離焦系列中晶格影像不再隨離焦反轉對比。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record a defocus series on amorphous carbon and Fourier-transform each image: the Thon-ring radii give the CTF zeros and fitting χ(u) solves Δf and C_s together; measure C_s, coma and threefold astigmatism with a Zemlin tableau of Thon rings at several beam tilts; after correction re-record and confirm the first zero has moved beyond 0.1 nm and lattice images no longer reverse contrast across the defocus series.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Scherzer 點解析度 d_S = 0.66·(C_s·λ³)^¼，Scherzer 離焦 Δf_S = −1.2·√(C_s·λ)。300 kV、λ = 1.97 pm：C_s = 0.6 mm 給 d_S = 0.17 nm、Δf_S = −41 nm；C_s = 1.2 mm 給 0.20 nm、−58 nm。最佳物鏡光圈半角 α ≈ (4λ/C_s)^¼ ≈ 10.7 mrad。校正器把 C_s 壓到 µm 等級後，光圈由五階像差 C₅ 限制，C₅ = 5 mm 時 α ≈ (λ/C₅)^⅙ ≈ 27 mrad，可接受的角度大了 2.5 倍，解析度改由資訊極限決定。","textEn":"Scherzer point resolution d_S = 0.66·(C_s·λ³)^¼ and Scherzer defocus Δf_S = −1.2·√(C_s·λ). At 300 kV with λ = 1.97 pm: C_s = 0.6 mm gives d_S = 0.17 nm and Δf_S = −41 nm; C_s = 1.2 mm gives 0.20 nm and −58 nm. The optimum objective semi-angle is α ≈ (4λ/C_s)^¼ ≈ 10.7 mrad. Once a corrector brings C_s to the micrometre level the aperture is limited by fifth-order aberration C₅: with C₅ = 5 mm, α ≈ (λ/C₅)^⅙ ≈ 27 mrad, 2.5 times the accepted angle, and resolution passes to the information limit.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「相位對比傳遞、Scherzer 解析度與 Cs 校正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Phase-contrast transfer, Scherzer resolution and Cs correction\", which statement holds?","options":["Scherzer 點解析度 d_S = 0.66·(C_s·λ³)^¼，Scherzer 離焦 Δf_S = −1.2·√(C_s·λ)。","軟體顯示的比例尺是絕對的，不需要用晶格校正。","顯微鏡放在地下室就自動滿足振動與磁場規格。"],"optionsEn":["Scherzer point resolution d_S = 0.66·(C_s·λ³)^¼ and Scherzer defocus Δf_S = −1.2·√(C_s·λ).","The scale bar shown by the software is absolute and needs no lattice calibration.","Putting the microscope in a basement automatically satisfies vibration and field specifications."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Scherzer 點解析度 d_S = 0.66·(C_s·λ³)^¼，Scherzer 離焦 Δf_S = −1.2·√(C_s·λ)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Scherzer point resolution d_S = 0.66·(C_s·λ³)^¼ and Scherzer defocus Δf_S = −1.2·√(C_s·λ). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"a442-v12-07","title":"相位對比傳遞、Scherzer 解析度與 Cs 校正：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Phase-contrast transfer, Scherzer resolution and Cs correction: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「對比傳遞函數與 Scherzer 離焦」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Contrast transfer function and Scherzer defocus” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"在非晶碳膜上拍一系列離焦影像並對每張做傅立葉轉換，Thon 環的半徑序列給出 CTF 的過零點，擬合 χ(u) 可同時解出 Δf 與 C_s；用 Zemlin 離焦傾斜表（在不同束傾角下的 Thon 環）量 C_s、彗差與三重像散；校正後重拍，確認第一過零點移到 0.1 nm 以外且離焦系列中晶格影像不再隨離焦反轉對比。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record a defocus series on amorphous carbon and Fourier-transform each image: the Thon-ring radii give the CTF zeros and fitting χ(u) solves Δf and C_s together; measure C_s, coma and threefold astigmatism with a Zemlin tableau of Thon rings at several beam tilts; after correction re-record and confirm the first zero has moved beyond 0.1 nm and lattice images no longer reverse contrast across the defocus series. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：未校正的顯微鏡在離焦偏離 Scherzer 值 30 nm 時，晶格影像的原子位置與真實位置互換（對比反轉），分析者把亮點當原子柱而把空隙當原子，導出錯誤的介面結構。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: An uncorrected microscope defocused 30 nm away from the Scherzer value swaps bright and dark lattice positions (contrast reversal); the analyst takes bright spots for atomic columns and gaps for atoms and derives a wrong interface structure.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在非晶碳膜上拍一系列離焦影像並對每張做傅立葉轉換，Thon 環的半徑序列給出 CTF 的過零點，擬合 χ(u) 可同時解出 Δf 與 C_s；用 Zemlin 離焦傾斜表（在不同束傾角下的 Thon 環）量 C_s、彗差與三重像散；校正後重拍，確認第一過零點移到 0.1 nm 以外且離焦系列中晶格影像不再隨離焦反轉對比。","textEn":"Record a defocus series on amorphous carbon and Fourier-transform each image: the Thon-ring radii give the CTF zeros and fitting χ(u) solves Δf and C_s together; measure C_s, coma and threefold astigmatism with a Zemlin tableau of Thon rings at several beam tilts; after correction re-record and confirm the first zero has moved beyond 0.1 nm and lattice images no longer reverse contrast across the defocus series.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-07-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「相位對比傳遞、Scherzer 解析度與 Cs 校正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Phase-contrast transfer, Scherzer resolution and Cs correction\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","在非晶碳膜上拍一系列離焦影像並對每張做傅立葉轉換，Thon 環的半徑序列給出 CTF 的過零點，擬合 χ(u) 可同時解出 Δf 與 C_s。","規格表上的解析度就是日常使用時可達到的解析度。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Record a defocus series on amorphous carbon and Fourier-transform each image: the Thon-ring radii give the CTF zeros and fitting χ(u) solves Δf and C_s together.","The resolution on the specification sheet is the resolution achieved in daily use."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在非晶碳膜上拍一系列離焦影像並對每張做傅立葉轉換，Thon 環的半徑序列給出 CTF 的過零點，擬合 χ(u) 可同時解出 Δf 與 C_s；用 Zemlin 離焦傾斜表（在不同束傾角下的 Thon 環）量 C_s、彗差與三重像散；校正後重拍，確認第一過零點移到 0.1 nm 以外且離焦系列中晶格影像不再隨離焦反轉對比。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record a defocus series on amorphous carbon and Fourier-transform each image: the Thon-ring radii give the CTF zeros and fitting χ(u) solves Δf and C_s together; measure C_s, coma and threefold astigmatism with a Zemlin tableau of Thon rings at several beam tilts; after correction re-record and confirm the first zero has moved beyond 0.1 nm and lattice images no longer reverse contrast across the defocus series. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"a442-v12-08","title":"相位對比傳遞、Scherzer 解析度與 Cs 校正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Phase-contrast transfer, Scherzer resolution and Cs correction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「對比傳遞函數與 Scherzer 離焦」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Contrast transfer function and Scherzer defocus” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"未校正的顯微鏡在離焦偏離 Scherzer 值 30 nm 時，晶格影像的原子位置與真實位置互換（對比反轉），分析者把亮點當原子柱而把空隙當原子，導出錯誤的介面結構。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"An uncorrected microscope defocused 30 nm away from the Scherzer value swaps bright and dark lattice positions (contrast reversal); the analyst takes bright spots for atomic columns and gaps for atoms and derives a wrong interface structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：六極或八極 Cs 校正器產生負的球面像差抵銷物鏡的正值，使 C_s 可調到接近零甚至微負，過零點外推到色像差資訊極限，解析度由 0.17 nm 進入 0.1 nm 以下，並消除離域效應。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A hexapole or octupole Cs corrector produces negative spherical aberration to cancel the objective's positive value, letting C_s be tuned near zero or slightly negative, pushing the first zero out to the chromatic information limit, taking resolution from 0.17 nm to below 0.1 nm and removing delocalisation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「Cs 校正後解析度只受電子波長限制，可以達到皮米。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"After Cs correction resolution is limited only by electron wavelength and reaches picometres.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未校正的顯微鏡在離焦偏離 Scherzer 值 30 nm 時，晶格影像的原子位置與真實位置互換（對比反轉），分析者把亮點當原子柱而把空隙當原子，導出錯誤的介面結構。","textEn":"An uncorrected microscope defocused 30 nm away from the Scherzer value swaps bright and dark lattice positions (contrast reversal); the analyst takes bright spots for atomic columns and gaps for atoms and derives a wrong interface structure.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「相位對比傳遞、Scherzer 解析度與 Cs 校正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Phase-contrast transfer, Scherzer resolution and Cs correction\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","只要像差校正器調好，電子槍的能量散佈就無關緊要。","未校正的顯微鏡在離焦偏離 Scherzer 值 30 nm 時，晶格影像的原子位置與真實位置互換（對比反轉），分析者把亮點當原子柱而把空隙當原子，導出錯誤的介面結構。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","Once the corrector is tuned, the gun's energy spread no longer matters.","An uncorrected microscope defocused 30 nm away from the Scherzer value swaps bright and dark lattice positions (contrast reversal)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"未校正的顯微鏡在離焦偏離 Scherzer 值 30 nm 時，晶格影像的原子位置與真實位置互換（對比反轉），分析者把亮點當原子柱而把空隙當原子，導出錯誤的介面結構。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An uncorrected microscope defocused 30 nm away from the Scherzer value swaps bright and dark lattice positions (contrast reversal); the analyst takes bright spots for atomic columns and gaps for atoms and derives a wrong interface structure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"a442-v12-s2","title":"元件、材料與製造","titleEn":"Components, materials and fabrication","description":"本階段聚焦「電子槍、高壓穩定度與資訊極限」與「物鏡、校正器、樣品載台與偵測器」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Electron gun, high-voltage stability and the information limit\" and \"Objective lens, corrector, specimen holder and detectors\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a442-v12-09","title":"電子槍、高壓穩定度與資訊極限：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Electron gun, high-voltage stability and the information limit: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-08"],"objective":"說明「高壓槽、Schottky 槍與單色器」如何決定穿透電子顯微鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “High-voltage tank, Schottky gun and monochromator” determines the key performance of “Transmission electron microscopes”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"校正球面像差後，解析度受色像差控制的時間相干性限制：電子能量散佈 ΔE、高壓漣波 ΔV/V 與物鏡電流漣波 ΔI/I 都讓焦距抖動，疊加成焦距散佈 Δ = C_c·√((ΔE/E)² + (ΔV/V)² + (2ΔI/I)²)，高頻資訊因此被阻尼包絡壓掉。所以 300 kV 的高壓發生器放在絕緣氣體槽內以 ppm 等級穩壓，透鏡電源用高精度電流源與恆溫，Schottky 槍的 0.7 eV 散佈成為最大項；需要更高極限時加單色器把散佈壓到 0.2 eV 以下，代價是損失大部分電流。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「高壓槽、Schottky 槍與單色器」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"With spherical aberration corrected, resolution is bounded by temporal coherence governed by chromatic aberration: energy spread ΔE, high-voltage ripple ΔV/V and objective-current ripple ΔI/I each jitter the focus and combine into a focal spread Δ = C_c·√((ΔE/E)² + (ΔV/V)² + (2ΔI/I)²), and a damping envelope suppresses high-frequency information. The 300 kV generator therefore sits in an insulating-gas tank regulated at the ppm level, lens supplies use precision current sources in temperature-controlled housings, and the 0.7 eV spread of a Schottky gun becomes the largest term; a monochromator brings the spread below 0.2 eV when a higher limit is needed, at the cost of most of the current. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “High-voltage tank, Schottky gun and monochromator”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：資訊極限 d_info ≈ √(πλΔ/2)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Information limit d_info ≈ √(πλΔ/2).","failure":"常見誤解：「只要像差校正器調好，電子槍的能量散佈就無關緊要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once the corrector is tuned, the gun's energy spread no longer matters.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「高壓槽、Schottky 槍與單色器」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “High-voltage tank, Schottky gun and monochromator”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-09-k1","title":"電子槍、高壓穩定度與資訊極限","titleEn":"Electron gun, high-voltage stability and the information limit","text":"校正球面像差後，解析度受色像差控制的時間相干性限制：電子能量散佈 ΔE、高壓漣波 ΔV/V 與物鏡電流漣波 ΔI/I 都讓焦距抖動，疊加成焦距散佈 Δ = C_c·√((ΔE/E)² + (ΔV/V)² + (2ΔI/I)²)，高頻資訊因此被阻尼包絡壓掉。所以 300 kV 的高壓發生器放在絕緣氣體槽內以 ppm 等級穩壓，透鏡電源用高精度電流源與恆溫，Schottky 槍的 0.7 eV 散佈成為最大項；需要更高極限時加單色器把散佈壓到 0.2 eV 以下，代價是損失大部分電流。","textEn":"With spherical aberration corrected, resolution is bounded by temporal coherence governed by chromatic aberration: energy spread ΔE, high-voltage ripple ΔV/V and objective-current ripple ΔI/I each jitter the focus and combine into a focal spread Δ = C_c·√((ΔE/E)² + (ΔV/V)² + (2ΔI/I)²), and a damping envelope suppresses high-frequency information. The 300 kV generator therefore sits in an insulating-gas tank regulated at the ppm level, lens supplies use precision current sources in temperature-controlled housings, and the 0.7 eV spread of a Schottky gun becomes the largest term; a monochromator brings the spread below 0.2 eV when a higher limit is needed, at the cost of most of the current.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要像差校正器調好，電子槍的能量散佈就無關緊要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once the corrector is tuned, the gun's energy spread no longer matters. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電子槍、高壓穩定度與資訊極限」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Electron gun, high-voltage stability and the information limit\" is correct?","options":["校正球面像差後，解析度受色像差控制的時間相干性限制：電子能量散佈 ΔE、高壓漣波 ΔV/V 與物鏡電流漣波 ΔI/I 都讓焦距抖動，疊加成焦距散佈 Δ = C_c·√((ΔE/E)² + (ΔV/V)² + (2ΔI/I)²)，高頻資訊因此被阻尼包絡壓掉。","只要像差校正器調好，電子槍的能量散佈就無關緊要。","極靴間隙越小越好，因為像差係數更低。"],"optionsEn":["With spherical aberration corrected, resolution is bounded by temporal coherence governed by chromatic aberration: energy spread ΔE, high-voltage ripple ΔV/V and objective-current ripple ΔI/I each jitter the focus and combine into a focal spread Δ = C_c·√((ΔE/E)² + (ΔV/V)² + (2ΔI/I)²), and a damping envelope suppresses high-frequency information.","Once the corrector is tuned, the gun's energy spread no longer matters.","A smaller pole-piece gap is always better because aberration coefficients are lower."],"answer":0,"explanation":"校正球面像差後，解析度受色像差控制的時間相干性限制：電子能量散佈 ΔE、高壓漣波 ΔV/V 與物鏡電流漣波 ΔI/I 都讓焦距抖動，疊加成焦距散佈 Δ = C_c·√((ΔE/E)² + (ΔV/V)² + (2ΔI/I)²)，高頻資訊因此被阻尼包絡壓掉。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"With spherical aberration corrected, resolution is bounded by temporal coherence governed by chromatic aberration: energy spread ΔE, high-voltage ripple ΔV/V and objective-current ripple ΔI/I each jitter the focus and combine into a focal spread Δ = C_c·√((ΔE/E)² + (ΔV/V)² + (2ΔI/I)²), and a damping envelope suppresses high-frequency information. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"a442-v12-10","title":"電子槍、高壓穩定度與資訊極限：定量估算","titleEn":"Electron gun, high-voltage stability and the information limit: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高壓槽、Schottky 槍與單色器」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “High-voltage tank, Schottky gun and monochromator” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：資訊極限 d_info ≈ √(πλΔ/2)。300 kV、C_c = 1.4 mm、ΔV/V = 1 ppm、ΔI/I = 0.5 ppm：Schottky ΔE = 0.7 eV（含相對論修正）給 Δ ≈ 4.5 nm，d_info ≈ 0.12 nm；單色器 ΔE = 0.2 eV 給 Δ ≈ 2.3 nm，d_info ≈ 0.084 nm。若高壓穩定度退化到 10 ppm，Δ 升到約 14 nm，d_info 退回 0.21 nm，比未校正的 Scherzer 解析度還差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Information limit d_info ≈ √(πλΔ/2). At 300 kV with C_c = 1.4 mm, ΔV/V = 1 ppm and ΔI/I = 0.5 ppm: a Schottky ΔE = 0.7 eV (with relativistic correction) gives Δ ≈ 4.5 nm and d_info ≈ 0.12 nm; a monochromator at ΔE = 0.2 eV gives Δ ≈ 2.3 nm and d_info ≈ 0.084 nm. If high-voltage stability degrades to 10 ppm, Δ rises to about 14 nm and d_info falls back to 0.21 nm, worse than the uncorrected Scherzer resolution. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：用電子能量損失譜儀量零損失峰的半高寬得到 ΔE；用 Young 條紋法（同一區域兩張小位移影像的傅立葉轉換）量資訊極限；監視高壓槽的分壓回授與物鏡電流的長時間紀錄，統計 ppm 級的漣波與漂移；把量到的三項代入 Δ 公式，預測的 d_info 應與 Young 條紋結果一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure ΔE from the zero-loss-peak width in electron energy-loss spectroscopy; measure the information limit by Young's fringes (Fourier transform of two slightly shifted images of one area); log the high-voltage divider feedback and objective current over long periods to quantify ppm ripple and drift; insert the three terms into the Δ formula and the predicted d_info should match the Young's-fringe result.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"資訊極限 d_info ≈ √(πλΔ/2)。300 kV、C_c = 1.4 mm、ΔV/V = 1 ppm、ΔI/I = 0.5 ppm：Schottky ΔE = 0.7 eV（含相對論修正）給 Δ ≈ 4.5 nm，d_info ≈ 0.12 nm；單色器 ΔE = 0.2 eV 給 Δ ≈ 2.3 nm，d_info ≈ 0.084 nm。若高壓穩定度退化到 10 ppm，Δ 升到約 14 nm，d_info 退回 0.21 nm，比未校正的 Scherzer 解析度還差。","textEn":"Information limit d_info ≈ √(πλΔ/2). At 300 kV with C_c = 1.4 mm, ΔV/V = 1 ppm and ΔI/I = 0.5 ppm: a Schottky ΔE = 0.7 eV (with relativistic correction) gives Δ ≈ 4.5 nm and d_info ≈ 0.12 nm; a monochromator at ΔE = 0.2 eV gives Δ ≈ 2.3 nm and d_info ≈ 0.084 nm. If high-voltage stability degrades to 10 ppm, Δ rises to about 14 nm and d_info falls back to 0.21 nm, worse than the uncorrected Scherzer resolution.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「電子槍、高壓穩定度與資訊極限」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Electron gun, high-voltage stability and the information limit\", which statement holds?","options":["加速電壓越高穿透力越強，所以總是對樣品更溫和。","資訊極限 d_info ≈ √(πλΔ/2)。","規格表上的解析度就是日常使用時可達到的解析度。"],"optionsEn":["Higher accelerating voltage penetrates better and is therefore always gentler on the specimen.","Information limit d_info ≈ √(πλΔ/2).","The resolution on the specification sheet is the resolution achieved in daily use."],"answer":1,"explanation":"資訊極限 d_info ≈ √(πλΔ/2)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Information limit d_info ≈ √(πλΔ/2). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"a442-v12-11","title":"電子槍、高壓穩定度與資訊極限：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Electron gun, high-voltage stability and the information limit: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「高壓槽、Schottky 槍與單色器」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “High-voltage tank, Schottky gun and monochromator” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"用電子能量損失譜儀量零損失峰的半高寬得到 ΔE；用 Young 條紋法（同一區域兩張小位移影像的傅立葉轉換）量資訊極限；監視高壓槽的分壓回授與物鏡電流的長時間紀錄，統計 ppm 級的漣波與漂移；把量到的三項代入 Δ 公式，預測的 d_info 應與 Young 條紋結果一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure ΔE from the zero-loss-peak width in electron energy-loss spectroscopy; measure the information limit by Young's fringes (Fourier transform of two slightly shifted images of one area); log the high-voltage divider feedback and objective current over long periods to quantify ppm ripple and drift; insert the three terms into the Δ formula and the predicted d_info should match the Young's-fringe result. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：高壓槽的分壓電阻受潮後穩定度從 1 ppm 退到 10 ppm，校正器調得再好晶格影像也只到 0.2 nm，操作者反覆重調校正器數日，直到看 Young 條紋才發現極限來自高壓而非像差。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A damp divider resistor degrades high-voltage stability from 1 to 10 ppm; however well the corrector is tuned, lattice images stop at 0.2 nm, and the operator re-tunes the corrector for days until Young's fringes show the limit comes from the high voltage, not aberrations.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用電子能量損失譜儀量零損失峰的半高寬得到 ΔE；用 Young 條紋法（同一區域兩張小位移影像的傅立葉轉換）量資訊極限；監視高壓槽的分壓回授與物鏡電流的長時間紀錄，統計 ppm 級的漣波與漂移；把量到的三項代入 Δ 公式，預測的 d_info 應與 Young 條紋結果一致。","textEn":"Measure ΔE from the zero-loss-peak width in electron energy-loss spectroscopy; measure the information limit by Young's fringes (Fourier transform of two slightly shifted images of one area); log the high-voltage divider feedback and objective current over long periods to quantify ppm ripple and drift; insert the three terms into the Δ formula and the predicted d_info should match the Young's-fringe result.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-11-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「電子槍、高壓穩定度與資訊極限」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Electron gun, high-voltage stability and the information limit\"?","options":["只看單次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準件或重複量測。","穿透電子顯微鏡的影像對比和光學顯微鏡一樣來自吸收。","用電子能量損失譜儀量零損失峰的半高寬得到 ΔE。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the result; no reference artefact or repeat measurement is needed.","TEM image contrast comes from absorption, as in a light microscope.","Measure ΔE from the zero-loss-peak width in electron energy-loss spectroscopy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用電子能量損失譜儀量零損失峰的半高寬得到 ΔE；用 Young 條紋法（同一區域兩張小位移影像的傅立葉轉換）量資訊極限；監視高壓槽的分壓回授與物鏡電流的長時間紀錄，統計 ppm 級的漣波與漂移；把量到的三項代入 Δ 公式，預測的 d_info 應與 Young 條紋結果一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure ΔE from the zero-loss-peak width in electron energy-loss spectroscopy; measure the information limit by Young's fringes (Fourier transform of two slightly shifted images of one area); log the high-voltage divider feedback and objective current over long periods to quantify ppm ripple and drift; insert the three terms into the Δ formula and the predicted d_info should match the Young's-fringe result. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"a442-v12-12","title":"電子槍、高壓穩定度與資訊極限：失效診斷","titleEn":"Electron gun, high-voltage stability and the information limit: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高壓槽、Schottky 槍與單色器」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “High-voltage tank, Schottky gun and monochromator” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"高壓槽的分壓電阻受潮後穩定度從 1 ppm 退到 10 ppm，校正器調得再好晶格影像也只到 0.2 nm，操作者反覆重調校正器數日，直到看 Young 條紋才發現極限來自高壓而非像差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A damp divider resistor degrades high-voltage stability from 1 to 10 ppm; however well the corrector is tuned, lattice images stop at 0.2 nm, and the operator re-tunes the corrector for days until Young's fringes show the limit comes from the high voltage, not aberrations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：所以 300 kV 的高壓發生器放在絕緣氣體槽內以 ppm 等級穩壓，透鏡電源用高精度電流源與恆溫，Schottky 槍的 0.7 eV 散佈成為最大項；需要更高極限時加單色器把散佈壓到 0.2 eV 以下，代價是損失大部分電流。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The 300 kV generator therefore sits in an insulating-gas tank regulated at the ppm level, lens supplies use precision current sources in temperature-controlled housings, and the 0.7 eV spread of a Schottky gun becomes the largest term; a monochromator brings the spread below 0.2 eV when a higher limit is needed, at the cost of most of the current.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要像差校正器調好，電子槍的能量散佈就無關緊要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once the corrector is tuned, the gun's energy spread no longer matters.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高壓槽的分壓電阻受潮後穩定度從 1 ppm 退到 10 ppm，校正器調得再好晶格影像也只到 0.2 nm，操作者反覆重調校正器數日，直到看 Young 條紋才發現極限來自高壓而非像差。","textEn":"A damp divider resistor degrades high-voltage stability from 1 to 10 ppm; however well the corrector is tuned, lattice images stop at 0.2 nm, and the operator re-tunes the corrector for days until Young's fringes show the limit comes from the high voltage, not aberrations.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電子槍、高壓穩定度與資訊極限」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Electron gun, high-voltage stability and the information limit\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["高壓槽的分壓電阻受潮後穩定度從 1 ppm 退到 10 ppm，校正器調得再好晶格影像也只到 0.2 nm，操作者反覆重調校正器數日，直到看 Young 條紋才發現極限來自高壓而非像差。","異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","極靴間隙越小越好，因為像差係數更低。"],"optionsEn":["A damp divider resistor degrades high-voltage stability from 1 to 10 ppm.","An anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A smaller pole-piece gap is always better because aberration coefficients are lower."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高壓槽的分壓電阻受潮後穩定度從 1 ppm 退到 10 ppm，校正器調得再好晶格影像也只到 0.2 nm，操作者反覆重調校正器數日，直到看 Young 條紋才發現極限來自高壓而非像差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A damp divider resistor degrades high-voltage stability from 1 to 10 ppm; however well the corrector is tuned, lattice images stop at 0.2 nm, and the operator re-tunes the corrector for days until Young's fringes show the limit comes from the high voltage, not aberrations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"a442-v12-13","title":"物鏡、校正器、樣品載台與偵測器：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Objective lens, corrector, specimen holder and detectors: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-12"],"objective":"說明「物鏡極靴、六極校正器與直接偵測器」如何決定穿透電子顯微鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Objective pole piece, hexapole corrector and direct detector” determines the key performance of “Transmission electron microscopes”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"物鏡的 C_s 與 C_c 隨極靴間隙縮小而降低，但間隙也限制樣品傾轉角度與分析偵測器的空間，高解析極靴通常只允許 ±20° 到 ±35° 的傾轉。校正器由兩組六極與傳遞透鏡組成，六極產生的三階負球面像差抵銷物鏡，但同時引入必須以多個偏轉與弱透鏡抵銷的寄生像差，整組需要數十個電源在毫安等級下保持 ppm 穩定。樣品載台在真空中以側插式桿承載，熱漂移與機械鬆弛決定曝光期間的位移。偵測器從閃爍體耦合 CMOS 走向直接電子偵測，後者以計數模式把偵測量子效率提升到接近 1，並允許以短幀對齊消除漂移。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「物鏡極靴、六極校正器與直接偵測器」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Objective C_s and C_c fall as the pole-piece gap shrinks, but the gap also limits specimen tilt and room for analytical detectors, so high-resolution pole pieces usually allow only ±20° to ±35° of tilt. The corrector consists of two hexapole groups with transfer lenses; the hexapoles create negative third-order spherical aberration that cancels the objective's, but introduce parasitic aberrations that must be nulled with many deflectors and weak lenses, so dozens of supplies must stay ppm-stable at milliamp levels. The specimen rides a side-entry holder in vacuum, and its thermal drift and mechanical relaxation set the displacement during exposure. Detectors have moved from scintillator-coupled CMOS to direct electron detection, whose counting mode raises detective quantum efficiency toward 1 and allows drift removal by aligning short frames. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Objective pole piece, hexapole corrector and direct detector”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：物鏡電流穩定度換算離焦：Δf/f ≈ 2ΔI/I，焦距 f = 2 mm、ΔI/I = 1 ppm → 4 nm 離焦抖動，與 −41 nm 的 Scherzer 離焦相比可接受；10 ppm 給 40 nm，晶格影像對比反轉。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Objective-current stability maps into defocus by Δf/f ≈ 2ΔI/I: with f = 2 mm and ΔI/I = 1 ppm the defocus jitters by 4 nm, acceptable against the −41 nm Scherzer value; 10 ppm gives 40 nm and lattice contrast reverses.","failure":"常見誤解：「極靴間隙越小越好，因為像差係數更低。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A smaller pole-piece gap is always better because aberration coefficients are lower.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「物鏡極靴、六極校正器與直接偵測器」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Objective pole piece, hexapole corrector and direct detector”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-13-k1","title":"物鏡、校正器、樣品載台與偵測器","titleEn":"Objective lens, corrector, specimen holder and detectors","text":"物鏡的 C_s 與 C_c 隨極靴間隙縮小而降低，但間隙也限制樣品傾轉角度與分析偵測器的空間，高解析極靴通常只允許 ±20° 到 ±35° 的傾轉。校正器由兩組六極與傳遞透鏡組成，六極產生的三階負球面像差抵銷物鏡，但同時引入必須以多個偏轉與弱透鏡抵銷的寄生像差，整組需要數十個電源在毫安等級下保持 ppm 穩定。","textEn":"Objective C_s and C_c fall as the pole-piece gap shrinks, but the gap also limits specimen tilt and room for analytical detectors, so high-resolution pole pieces usually allow only ±20° to ±35° of tilt. The corrector consists of two hexapole groups with transfer lenses; the hexapoles create negative third-order spherical aberration that cancels the objective's, but introduce parasitic aberrations that must be nulled with many deflectors and weak lenses, so dozens of supplies must stay ppm-stable at milliamp levels.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：極靴間隙越小越好，因為像差係數更低。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A smaller pole-piece gap is always better because aberration coefficients are lower. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「物鏡、校正器、樣品載台與偵測器」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Objective lens, corrector, specimen holder and detectors\" is correct?","options":["極靴間隙越小越好，因為像差係數更低。","物鏡的 C_s 與 C_c 隨極靴間隙縮小而降低，但間隙也限制樣品傾轉角度與分析偵測器的空間，高解析極靴通常只允許 ±20° 到 ±35° 的傾轉。","軟體顯示的比例尺是絕對的，不需要用晶格校正。"],"optionsEn":["A smaller pole-piece gap is always better because aberration coefficients are lower.","Objective C_s and C_c fall as the pole-piece gap shrinks, but the gap also limits specimen tilt and room for analytical detectors, so high-resolution pole pieces usually allow only ±20° to ±35° of tilt.","The scale bar shown by the software is absolute and needs no lattice calibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"物鏡的 C_s 與 C_c 隨極靴間隙縮小而降低，但間隙也限制樣品傾轉角度與分析偵測器的空間，高解析極靴通常只允許 ±20° 到 ±35° 的傾轉。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Objective C_s and C_c fall as the pole-piece gap shrinks, but the gap also limits specimen tilt and room for analytical detectors, so high-resolution pole pieces usually allow only ±20° to ±35° of tilt. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"a442-v12-14","title":"物鏡、校正器、樣品載台與偵測器：定量估算","titleEn":"Objective lens, corrector, specimen holder and detectors: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「物鏡極靴、六極校正器與直接偵測器」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Objective pole piece, hexapole corrector and direct detector” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：物鏡電流穩定度換算離焦：Δf/f ≈ 2ΔI/I，焦距 f = 2 mm、ΔI/I = 1 ppm → 4 nm 離焦抖動，與 −41 nm 的 Scherzer 離焦相比可接受；10 ppm 給 40 nm，晶格影像對比反轉。載台漂移 0.5 nm/min 在 2 s 曝光中位移 0.017 nm，對 0.1 nm 解析度仍可接受，但 5 nm/min 就會把啞鈴抹成一條。直接偵測器在 1 nA、直徑 1 µm 的照明下劑量率約 8×10³ e/nm²/s，計數模式需把每像素每幀的電子數壓在 0.1 以下以避免重合損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Objective-current stability maps into defocus by Δf/f ≈ 2ΔI/I: with f = 2 mm and ΔI/I = 1 ppm the defocus jitters by 4 nm, acceptable against the −41 nm Scherzer value; 10 ppm gives 40 nm and lattice contrast reverses. Holder drift of 0.5 nm/min moves 0.017 nm during a 2 s exposure, still acceptable at 0.1 nm resolution, but 5 nm/min smears dumbbells into a line. A direct detector under 1 nA in a 1 µm illuminated disc sees about 8×10³ e/nm²/s, and counting mode needs fewer than 0.1 electrons per pixel per frame to avoid coincidence loss. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以金顆粒影像序列的互相關量載台漂移曲線，決定插入後的等待時間；用校正器軟體的像差表（A1、B2、C3、A3 等）確認殘餘像差在目標解析度對應的 π/4 相位容限內；偵測器以均勻照明量增益與雜訊，計算各劑量率下的 DQE(0) 與調制傳遞函數，確認計數模式的線性範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Cross-correlate a gold-particle image series to get the holder drift curve and set the settling time after insertion; use the corrector software's aberration table (A1, B2, C3, A3 and so on) to confirm residual aberrations lie within the π/4 phase tolerance for the target resolution; characterise the detector under uniform illumination for gain and noise, compute DQE(0) and modulation transfer function at several dose rates, and establish the linear range of counting mode.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"物鏡電流穩定度換算離焦：Δf/f ≈ 2ΔI/I，焦距 f = 2 mm、ΔI/I = 1 ppm → 4 nm 離焦抖動，與 −41 nm 的 Scherzer 離焦相比可接受；10 ppm 給 40 nm，晶格影像對比反轉。載台漂移 0.5 nm/min 在 2 s 曝光中位移 0.017 nm，對 0.1 nm 解析度仍可接受，但 5 nm/min 就會把啞鈴抹成一條。直接偵測器在 1 nA、直徑 1 µm 的照明下劑量率約 8×10³ e/nm²/s，計數模式需把每像素每幀的電子數壓在 0.1 以下以避免重合損失。","textEn":"Objective-current stability maps into defocus by Δf/f ≈ 2ΔI/I: with f = 2 mm and ΔI/I = 1 ppm the defocus jitters by 4 nm, acceptable against the −41 nm Scherzer value; 10 ppm gives 40 nm and lattice contrast reverses. Holder drift of 0.5 nm/min moves 0.017 nm during a 2 s exposure, still acceptable at 0.1 nm resolution, but 5 nm/min smears dumbbells into a line. A direct detector under 1 nA in a 1 µm illuminated disc sees about 8×10³ e/nm²/s, and counting mode needs fewer than 0.1 electrons per pixel per frame to avoid coincidence loss.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「物鏡、校正器、樣品載台與偵測器」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Objective lens, corrector, specimen holder and detectors\", which statement holds?","options":["顯微鏡放在地下室就自動滿足振動與磁場規格。","穿透電子顯微鏡的影像對比和光學顯微鏡一樣來自吸收。","物鏡電流穩定度換算離焦：Δf/f ≈ 2ΔI/I，焦距 f = 2 mm、ΔI/I = 1 ppm → 4 nm 離焦抖動，與 −41 nm 的 Scherzer 離焦相比可接受。"],"optionsEn":["Putting the microscope in a basement automatically satisfies vibration and field specifications.","TEM image contrast comes from absorption, as in a light microscope.","Objective-current stability maps into defocus by Δf/f ≈ 2ΔI/I: with f = 2 mm and ΔI/I = 1 ppm the defocus jitters by 4 nm, acceptable against the −41 nm Scherzer value."],"answer":2,"explanation":"物鏡電流穩定度換算離焦：Δf/f ≈ 2ΔI/I，焦距 f = 2 mm、ΔI/I = 1 ppm → 4 nm 離焦抖動，與 −41 nm 的 Scherzer 離焦相比可接受；10 ppm 給 40 nm，晶格影像對比反轉。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Objective-current stability maps into defocus by Δf/f ≈ 2ΔI/I: with f = 2 mm and ΔI/I = 1 ppm the defocus jitters by 4 nm, acceptable against the −41 nm Scherzer value; 10 ppm gives 40 nm and lattice contrast reverses. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"a442-v12-15","title":"物鏡、校正器、樣品載台與偵測器：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Objective lens, corrector, specimen holder and detectors: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「物鏡極靴、六極校正器與直接偵測器」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Objective pole piece, hexapole corrector and direct detector” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以金顆粒影像序列的互相關量載台漂移曲線，決定插入後的等待時間；用校正器軟體的像差表（A1、B2、C3、A3 等）確認殘餘像差在目標解析度對應的 π/4 相位容限內；偵測器以均勻照明量增益與雜訊，計算各劑量率下的 DQE(0) 與調制傳遞函數，確認計數模式的線性範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Cross-correlate a gold-particle image series to get the holder drift curve and set the settling time after insertion; use the corrector software's aberration table (A1, B2, C3, A3 and so on) to confirm residual aberrations lie within the π/4 phase tolerance for the target resolution; characterise the detector under uniform illumination for gain and noise, compute DQE(0) and modulation transfer function at several dose rates, and establish the linear range of counting mode. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：校正器的某個六極電源溫度漂移使三重像散 A2 在 10 分鐘內跑到 100 nm，剛調好的 0.08 nm 條件在拍攝時已退化到 0.12 nm，資料看似正常卻無法重現，問題直到比對像差表時序才被找到。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A temperature drift in one hexapole supply lets threefold astigmatism A2 run to 100 nm within 10 minutes; the freshly tuned 0.08 nm condition has degraded to 0.12 nm by the time of recording, data look normal yet cannot be reproduced, and the cause is found only by comparing aberration-table time stamps.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以金顆粒影像序列的互相關量載台漂移曲線，決定插入後的等待時間；用校正器軟體的像差表（A1、B2、C3、A3 等）確認殘餘像差在目標解析度對應的 π/4 相位容限內；偵測器以均勻照明量增益與雜訊，計算各劑量率下的 DQE(0) 與調制傳遞函數，確認計數模式的線性範圍。","textEn":"Cross-correlate a gold-particle image series to get the holder drift curve and set the settling time after insertion; use the corrector software's aberration table (A1, B2, C3, A3 and so on) to confirm residual aberrations lie within the π/4 phase tolerance for the target resolution; characterise the detector under uniform illumination for gain and noise, compute DQE(0) and modulation transfer function at several dose rates, and establish the linear range of counting mode.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-15-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「物鏡、校正器、樣品載台與偵測器」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Objective lens, corrector, specimen holder and detectors\"?","options":["以金顆粒影像序列的互相關量載台漂移曲線，決定插入後的等待時間。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","Cs 校正後解析度只受電子波長限制，可以達到皮米。"],"optionsEn":["Cross-correlate a gold-particle image series to get the holder drift curve and set the settling time after insertion.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","After Cs correction resolution is limited only by electron wavelength and reaches picometres."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以金顆粒影像序列的互相關量載台漂移曲線，決定插入後的等待時間；用校正器軟體的像差表（A1、B2、C3、A3 等）確認殘餘像差在目標解析度對應的 π/4 相位容限內；偵測器以均勻照明量增益與雜訊，計算各劑量率下的 DQE(0) 與調制傳遞函數，確認計數模式的線性範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Cross-correlate a gold-particle image series to get the holder drift curve and set the settling time after insertion; use the corrector software's aberration table (A1, B2, C3, A3 and so on) to confirm residual aberrations lie within the π/4 phase tolerance for the target resolution; characterise the detector under uniform illumination for gain and noise, compute DQE(0) and modulation transfer function at several dose rates, and establish the linear range of counting mode. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"a442-v12-16","title":"物鏡、校正器、樣品載台與偵測器：失效診斷","titleEn":"Objective lens, corrector, specimen holder and detectors: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「物鏡極靴、六極校正器與直接偵測器」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Objective pole piece, hexapole corrector and direct detector” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"校正器的某個六極電源溫度漂移使三重像散 A2 在 10 分鐘內跑到 100 nm，剛調好的 0.08 nm 條件在拍攝時已退化到 0.12 nm，資料看似正常卻無法重現，問題直到比對像差表時序才被找到。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A temperature drift in one hexapole supply lets threefold astigmatism A2 run to 100 nm within 10 minutes; the freshly tuned 0.08 nm condition has degraded to 0.12 nm by the time of recording, data look normal yet cannot be reproduced, and the cause is found only by comparing aberration-table time stamps. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：偵測器從閃爍體耦合 CMOS 走向直接電子偵測，後者以計數模式把偵測量子效率提升到接近 1，並允許以短幀對齊消除漂移。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Detectors have moved from scintillator-coupled CMOS to direct electron detection, whose counting mode raises detective quantum efficiency toward 1 and allows drift removal by aligning short frames.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「極靴間隙越小越好，因為像差係數更低。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A smaller pole-piece gap is always better because aberration coefficients are lower.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"校正器的某個六極電源溫度漂移使三重像散 A2 在 10 分鐘內跑到 100 nm，剛調好的 0.08 nm 條件在拍攝時已退化到 0.12 nm，資料看似正常卻無法重現，問題直到比對像差表時序才被找到。","textEn":"A temperature drift in one hexapole supply lets threefold astigmatism A2 run to 100 nm within 10 minutes; the freshly tuned 0.08 nm condition has degraded to 0.12 nm by the time of recording, data look normal yet cannot be reproduced, and the cause is found only by comparing aberration-table time stamps.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「物鏡、校正器、樣品載台與偵測器」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Objective lens, corrector, specimen holder and detectors\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的零件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","校正器的某個六極電源溫度漂移使三重像散 A2 在 10 分鐘內跑到 100 nm，剛調好的 0.08 nm 條件在拍攝時已退化到 0.12 nm，資料看似正常卻無法重現，問題直到比對像差表時序才被找到。","軟體顯示的比例尺是絕對的，不需要用晶格校正。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive part first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A temperature drift in one hexapole supply lets threefold astigmatism A2 run to 100 nm within 10 minutes.","The scale bar shown by the software is absolute and needs no lattice calibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"校正器的某個六極電源溫度漂移使三重像散 A2 在 10 分鐘內跑到 100 nm，剛調好的 0.08 nm 條件在拍攝時已退化到 0.12 nm，資料看似正常卻無法重現，問題直到比對像差表時序才被找到。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A temperature drift in one hexapole supply lets threefold astigmatism A2 run to 100 nm within 10 minutes; the freshly tuned 0.08 nm condition has degraded to 0.12 nm by the time of recording, data look normal yet cannot be reproduced, and the cause is found only by comparing aberration-table time stamps. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"a442-v12-s3","title":"量測、校正與誤差預算","titleEn":"Measurement, calibration and error budgets","description":"本階段聚焦「放大率、相機長度與像差量測的校正」與「樣品厚度、非彈性散射與輻射損傷」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Calibrating magnification, camera length and aberration measurement\" and \"Specimen thickness, inelastic scattering and radiation damage\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a442-v12-17","title":"放大率、相機長度與像差量測的校正：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Calibrating magnification, camera length and aberration measurement: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-16"],"objective":"說明「矽晶格與金環校正樣品」如何決定穿透電子顯微鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Silicon lattice and gold-ring calibration specimens” determines the key performance of “Transmission electron microscopes”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"影像上的長度尺度由物鏡與投影鏡的激磁決定，隨放大率檔位、高壓與鏡體溫度變化，必須以晶格間距已知的樣品校正：高倍用矽 (111) 0.3136 nm 或 (220) 0.1920 nm 晶格條紋，中低倍用溝槽光柵複製膜或奈米顆粒標準片；繞射模式的相機長度用多晶金環校正。像差量測本身也要校正：Zemlin 表假設束傾角已知，而束傾角由偏轉線圈的校正係數決定，所以先用繞射點位移校正偏轉線圈，再量像差。所有校正值都綁定高壓、放大率檔位與極靴，換任一項就要重做。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「矽晶格與金環校正樣品」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Image scale depends on objective and projector excitation and changes with magnification step, high voltage and column temperature, so it is calibrated with specimens of known lattice spacing: silicon (111) 0.3136 nm or (220) 0.1920 nm fringes at high magnification, replica gratings or nanoparticle standards at lower magnification; camera length in diffraction mode is calibrated with polycrystalline gold rings. Aberration measurement must itself be calibrated: a Zemlin tableau assumes known beam tilts, which depend on deflector calibration coefficients, so deflectors are first calibrated from diffraction-spot shifts and only then are aberrations measured. Every calibration value is bound to high voltage, magnification step and pole piece, and changing any one requires redoing it. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Silicon lattice and gold-ring calibration specimens”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：相機長度校正：金 (111) 環在 L = 0.5 m 的半徑 4.18 mm，若實測 4.26 mm 則 L 偏差 1.9%，修正後殘餘由環半徑定位（0.02 mm → 0.5%）決定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Camera-length calibration: the gold (111) ring at L = 0.5 m has radius 4.18 mm; a measured 4.26 mm means L is off by 1.9%, and after correction the residual is set by ring-radius location (0.02 mm → 0.5%).","failure":"常見誤解：「軟體顯示的比例尺是絕對的，不需要用晶格校正。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The scale bar shown by the software is absolute and needs no lattice calibration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「矽晶格與金環校正樣品」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Silicon lattice and gold-ring calibration specimens”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-17-k1","title":"放大率、相機長度與像差量測的校正","titleEn":"Calibrating magnification, camera length and aberration measurement","text":"影像上的長度尺度由物鏡與投影鏡的激磁決定，隨放大率檔位、高壓與鏡體溫度變化，必須以晶格間距已知的樣品校正：高倍用矽 (111) 0.3136 nm 或 (220) 0.1920 nm 晶格條紋，中低倍用溝槽光柵複製膜或奈米顆粒標準片；繞射模式的相機長度用多晶金環校正。像差量測本身也要校正：Zemlin 表假設束傾角已知，而束傾角由偏轉線圈的校正係數決定，所以先用繞射點位移校正偏轉線圈，再量像差。","textEn":"Image scale depends on objective and projector excitation and changes with magnification step, high voltage and column temperature, so it is calibrated with specimens of known lattice spacing: silicon (111) 0.3136 nm or (220) 0.1920 nm fringes at high magnification, replica gratings or nanoparticle standards at lower magnification; camera length in diffraction mode is calibrated with polycrystalline gold rings. Aberration measurement must itself be calibrated: a Zemlin tableau assumes known beam tilts, which depend on deflector calibration coefficients, so deflectors are first calibrated from diffraction-spot shifts and only then are aberrations measured.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：軟體顯示的比例尺是絕對的，不需要用晶格校正。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The scale bar shown by the software is absolute and needs no lattice calibration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「放大率、相機長度與像差量測的校正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Calibrating magnification, camera length and aberration measurement\" is correct?","options":["軟體顯示的比例尺是絕對的，不需要用晶格校正。","加速電壓越高穿透力越強，所以總是對樣品更溫和。","影像上的長度尺度由物鏡與投影鏡的激磁決定，隨放大率檔位、高壓與鏡體溫度變化，必須以晶格間距已知的樣品校正：高倍用矽 (111) 0.3136 nm 或 (220) 0.1920 nm 晶格條紋，中低倍用溝槽光柵複製膜或奈米顆粒標準片。"],"optionsEn":["The scale bar shown by the software is absolute and needs no lattice calibration.","Higher accelerating voltage penetrates better and is therefore always gentler on the specimen.","Image scale depends on objective and projector excitation and changes with magnification step, high voltage and column temperature, so it is calibrated with specimens of known lattice spacing: silicon (111) 0.3136 nm or (220) 0.1920 nm fringes at high magnification, replica gratings or nanoparticle standards at lower magnification."],"answer":2,"explanation":"影像上的長度尺度由物鏡與投影鏡的激磁決定，隨放大率檔位、高壓與鏡體溫度變化，必須以晶格間距已知的樣品校正：高倍用矽 (111) 0.3136 nm 或 (220) 0.1920 nm 晶格條紋，中低倍用溝槽光柵複製膜或奈米顆粒標準片；繞射模式的相機長度用多晶金環校正。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Image scale depends on objective and projector excitation and changes with magnification step, high voltage and column temperature, so it is calibrated with specimens of known lattice spacing: silicon (111) 0.3136 nm or (220) 0.1920 nm fringes at high magnification, replica gratings or nanoparticle standards at lower magnification; camera length in diffraction mode is calibrated with polycrystalline gold rings. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"a442-v12-18","title":"放大率、相機長度與像差量測的校正：定量估算","titleEn":"Calibrating magnification, camera length and aberration measurement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「矽晶格與金環校正樣品」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Silicon lattice and gold-ring calibration specimens” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：相機長度校正：金 (111) 環在 L = 0.5 m 的半徑 4.18 mm，若實測 4.26 mm 則 L 偏差 1.9%，修正後殘餘由環半徑定位（0.02 mm → 0.5%）決定。放大率校正：矽 (111) 條紋 50 個週期應為 15.68 nm，實測像素數乘以標稱像素尺寸得 16.0 nm 時比例誤差 2%。偏轉線圈校正：束傾 10 mrad 應使繞射點移動 R = L·θ = 0.5 m×0.01 = 5 mm，偏差直接變成 Zemlin 表中 C_s 的比例誤差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Camera-length calibration: the gold (111) ring at L = 0.5 m has radius 4.18 mm; a measured 4.26 mm means L is off by 1.9%, and after correction the residual is set by ring-radius location (0.02 mm → 0.5%). Magnification: 50 periods of silicon (111) fringes should span 15.68 nm; if pixel count times nominal pixel size gives 16.0 nm the scale error is 2%. Deflector calibration: a 10 mrad beam tilt should move the diffraction spot by R = L·θ = 0.5 m×0.01 = 5 mm, and any deviation becomes a proportional error in the C_s from the Zemlin tableau. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：在每個常用放大率檔位拍矽晶格或光柵影像，由傅立葉轉換的峰位置算像素尺寸，建立放大率校正表並附高壓與日期；繞射模式對每個相機長度量金環；每季重複，比例漂移超過 1% 即重校；像差量測前先以繞射點位移校正束傾係數，再做 Zemlin 表，比較兩次獨立量測的 C_s 差異應小於 5%。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At every routinely used magnification step image silicon lattice or a grating, compute pixel size from Fourier peak positions and build a magnification table tagged with high voltage and date; measure gold rings for every camera length in diffraction mode; repeat quarterly and recalibrate when scale drifts beyond 1%; before aberration measurement calibrate beam-tilt coefficients from diffraction-spot shifts, then run the Zemlin tableau, and two independent C_s measurements should agree within 5%.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"相機長度校正：金 (111) 環在 L = 0.5 m 的半徑 4.18 mm，若實測 4.26 mm 則 L 偏差 1.9%，修正後殘餘由環半徑定位（0.02 mm → 0.5%）決定。放大率校正：矽 (111) 條紋 50 個週期應為 15.68 nm，實測像素數乘以標稱像素尺寸得 16.0 nm 時比例誤差 2%。偏轉線圈校正：束傾 10 mrad 應使繞射點移動 R = L·θ = 0.5 m×0.01 = 5 mm，偏差直接變成 Zemlin 表中 C_s 的比例誤差。","textEn":"Camera-length calibration: the gold (111) ring at L = 0.5 m has radius 4.18 mm; a measured 4.26 mm means L is off by 1.9%, and after correction the residual is set by ring-radius location (0.02 mm → 0.5%). Magnification: 50 periods of silicon (111) fringes should span 15.68 nm; if pixel count times nominal pixel size gives 16.0 nm the scale error is 2%. Deflector calibration: a 10 mrad beam tilt should move the diffraction spot by R = L·θ = 0.5 m×0.01 = 5 mm, and any deviation becomes a proportional error in the C_s from the Zemlin tableau.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「放大率、相機長度與像差量測的校正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Calibrating magnification, camera length and aberration measurement\", which statement holds?","options":["相機長度校正：金 (111) 環在 L = 0.5 m 的半徑 4.18 mm，若實測 4.26 mm 則 L 偏差 1.9%，修正後殘餘由環半徑定位（0.02 mm → 0.5%）決定。","規格表上的解析度就是日常使用時可達到的解析度。","Cs 校正後解析度只受電子波長限制，可以達到皮米。"],"optionsEn":["Camera-length calibration: the gold (111) ring at L = 0.5 m has radius 4.18 mm.","The resolution on the specification sheet is the resolution achieved in daily use.","After Cs correction resolution is limited only by electron wavelength and reaches picometres."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相機長度校正：金 (111) 環在 L = 0.5 m 的半徑 4.18 mm，若實測 4.26 mm 則 L 偏差 1.9%，修正後殘餘由環半徑定位（0.02 mm → 0.5%）決定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Camera-length calibration: the gold (111) ring at L = 0.5 m has radius 4.18 mm; a measured 4.26 mm means L is off by 1.9%, and after correction the residual is set by ring-radius location (0.02 mm → 0.5%). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"a442-v12-19","title":"放大率、相機長度與像差量測的校正：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Calibrating magnification, camera length and aberration measurement: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「矽晶格與金環校正樣品」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Silicon lattice and gold-ring calibration specimens” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"在每個常用放大率檔位拍矽晶格或光柵影像，由傅立葉轉換的峰位置算像素尺寸，建立放大率校正表並附高壓與日期；繞射模式對每個相機長度量金環；每季重複，比例漂移超過 1% 即重校；像差量測前先以繞射點位移校正束傾係數，再做 Zemlin 表，比較兩次獨立量測的 C_s 差異應小於 5%。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At every routinely used magnification step image silicon lattice or a grating, compute pixel size from Fourier peak positions and build a magnification table tagged with high voltage and date; measure gold rings for every camera length in diffraction mode; repeat quarterly and recalibrate when scale drifts beyond 1%; before aberration measurement calibrate beam-tilt coefficients from diffraction-spot shifts, then run the Zemlin tableau, and two independent C_s measurements should agree within 5%. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：用 200 kV 時建立的放大率表在切換到 300 kV 後繼續使用，透鏡激磁不同使比例差 4%，奈米顆粒粒徑統計全部偏小，論文發表後才被同行以 X 光繞射結果質疑。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A magnification table built at 200 kV is kept after switching to 300 kV; different lens excitation shifts the scale by 4%, every nanoparticle size statistic reads small, and the discrepancy is raised by peers with X-ray diffraction results only after publication.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在每個常用放大率檔位拍矽晶格或光柵影像，由傅立葉轉換的峰位置算像素尺寸，建立放大率校正表並附高壓與日期；繞射模式對每個相機長度量金環；每季重複，比例漂移超過 1% 即重校；像差量測前先以繞射點位移校正束傾係數，再做 Zemlin 表，比較兩次獨立量測的 C_s 差異應小於 5%。","textEn":"At every routinely used magnification step image silicon lattice or a grating, compute pixel size from Fourier peak positions and build a magnification table tagged with high voltage and date; measure gold rings for every camera length in diffraction mode; repeat quarterly and recalibrate when scale drifts beyond 1%; before aberration measurement calibrate beam-tilt coefficients from diffraction-spot shifts, then run the Zemlin tableau, and two independent C_s measurements should agree within 5%.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-19-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「放大率、相機長度與像差量測的校正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Calibrating magnification, camera length and aberration measurement\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在每個常用放大率檔位拍矽晶格或光柵影像，由傅立葉轉換的峰位置算像素尺寸，建立放大率校正表並附高壓與日期。","只要像差校正器調好，電子槍的能量散佈就無關緊要。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","At every routinely used magnification step image silicon lattice or a grating, compute pixel size from Fourier peak positions and build a magnification table tagged with high voltage and date.","Once the corrector is tuned, the gun's energy spread no longer matters."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在每個常用放大率檔位拍矽晶格或光柵影像，由傅立葉轉換的峰位置算像素尺寸，建立放大率校正表並附高壓與日期；繞射模式對每個相機長度量金環；每季重複，比例漂移超過 1% 即重校；像差量測前先以繞射點位移校正束傾係數，再做 Zemlin 表，比較兩次獨立量測的 C_s 差異應小於 5%。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"At every routinely used magnification step image silicon lattice or a grating, compute pixel size from Fourier peak positions and build a magnification table tagged with high voltage and date; measure gold rings for every camera length in diffraction mode; repeat quarterly and recalibrate when scale drifts beyond 1%; before aberration measurement calibrate beam-tilt coefficients from diffraction-spot shifts, then run the Zemlin tableau, and two independent C_s measurements should agree within 5%. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"a442-v12-20","title":"放大率、相機長度與像差量測的校正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Calibrating magnification, camera length and aberration measurement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「矽晶格與金環校正樣品」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Silicon lattice and gold-ring calibration specimens” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"用 200 kV 時建立的放大率表在切換到 300 kV 後繼續使用，透鏡激磁不同使比例差 4%，奈米顆粒粒徑統計全部偏小，論文發表後才被同行以 X 光繞射結果質疑。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A magnification table built at 200 kV is kept after switching to 300 kV; different lens excitation shifts the scale by 4%, every nanoparticle size statistic reads small, and the discrepancy is raised by peers with X-ray diffraction results only after publication. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：所有校正值都綁定高壓、放大率檔位與極靴，換任一項就要重做。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Every calibration value is bound to high voltage, magnification step and pole piece, and changing any one requires redoing it.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「軟體顯示的比例尺是絕對的，不需要用晶格校正。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The scale bar shown by the software is absolute and needs no lattice calibration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用 200 kV 時建立的放大率表在切換到 300 kV 後繼續使用，透鏡激磁不同使比例差 4%，奈米顆粒粒徑統計全部偏小，論文發表後才被同行以 X 光繞射結果質疑。","textEn":"A magnification table built at 200 kV is kept after switching to 300 kV; different lens excitation shifts the scale by 4%, every nanoparticle size statistic reads small, and the discrepancy is raised by peers with X-ray diffraction results only after publication.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「放大率、相機長度與像差量測的校正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Calibrating magnification, camera length and aberration measurement\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","加速電壓越高穿透力越強，所以總是對樣品更溫和。","用 200 kV 時建立的放大率表在切換到 300 kV 後繼續使用，透鏡激磁不同使比例差 4%，奈米顆粒粒徑統計全部偏小，論文發表後才被同行以 X 光繞射結果質疑。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Higher accelerating voltage penetrates better and is therefore always gentler on the specimen.","A magnification table built at 200 kV is kept after switching to 300 kV."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用 200 kV 時建立的放大率表在切換到 300 kV 後繼續使用，透鏡激磁不同使比例差 4%，奈米顆粒粒徑統計全部偏小，論文發表後才被同行以 X 光繞射結果質疑。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A magnification table built at 200 kV is kept after switching to 300 kV; different lens excitation shifts the scale by 4%, every nanoparticle size statistic reads small, and the discrepancy is raised by peers with X-ray diffraction results only after publication. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"a442-v12-21","title":"樣品厚度、非彈性散射與輻射損傷：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Specimen thickness, inelastic scattering and radiation damage: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-20"],"objective":"說明「樣品厚度、劑量與撞擊損傷」如何決定穿透電子顯微鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Specimen thickness, dose and knock-on damage” determines the key performance of “Transmission electron microscopes”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"高解析成像要求樣品厚度在 10 到 50 nm，電子在樣品內的非彈性平均自由徑約 100 nm 等級，厚度與自由徑之比 t/λ 可由能量損失譜的零損失峰與總強度之比求得，是每張影像都應記錄的參數。電子束同時損傷樣品：撞擊位移發生在電子能把超過位移閾值的能量傳給原子核時，最大傳遞能量隨加速電壓升高而增加，輕元素最敏感；電離損傷則對高分子與某些氧化物主導，隨電壓降低反而變嚴重。因此加速電壓是依樣品而選的參數，不是越高越好。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「樣品厚度、劑量與撞擊損傷」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"High-resolution imaging needs specimens 10 to 50 nm thick; the inelastic mean free path is of order 100 nm, and the ratio t/λ, obtained from the zero-loss to total intensity ratio in an energy-loss spectrum, is a parameter that should be recorded with every image. The beam also damages the specimen: knock-on displacement occurs when an electron can transfer more than the displacement threshold to a nucleus, and the maximum transferable energy rises with accelerating voltage, light elements being most sensitive; radiolysis dominates in polymers and some oxides and worsens as voltage falls. Accelerating voltage is therefore chosen per specimen, not simply maximised. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Specimen thickness, dose and knock-on damage”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：最大傳遞能量 E_max = 2E(E + 2m₀c²)/(Mc²)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Maximum transferred energy E_max = 2E(E + 2m₀c²)/(Mc²).","failure":"常見誤解：「加速電壓越高穿透力越強，所以總是對樣品更溫和。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher accelerating voltage penetrates better and is therefore always gentler on the specimen.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「樣品厚度、劑量與撞擊損傷」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Specimen thickness, dose and knock-on damage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-21-k1","title":"樣品厚度、非彈性散射與輻射損傷","titleEn":"Specimen thickness, inelastic scattering and radiation damage","text":"高解析成像要求樣品厚度在 10 到 50 nm，電子在樣品內的非彈性平均自由徑約 100 nm 等級，厚度與自由徑之比 t/λ 可由能量損失譜的零損失峰與總強度之比求得，是每張影像都應記錄的參數。電子束同時損傷樣品：撞擊位移發生在電子能把超過位移閾值的能量傳給原子核時，最大傳遞能量隨加速電壓升高而增加，輕元素最敏感；電離損傷則對高分子與某些氧化物主導，隨電壓降低反而變嚴重。","textEn":"High-resolution imaging needs specimens 10 to 50 nm thick; the inelastic mean free path is of order 100 nm, and the ratio t/λ, obtained from the zero-loss to total intensity ratio in an energy-loss spectrum, is a parameter that should be recorded with every image. The beam also damages the specimen: knock-on displacement occurs when an electron can transfer more than the displacement threshold to a nucleus, and the maximum transferable energy rises with accelerating voltage, light elements being most sensitive; radiolysis dominates in polymers and some oxides and worsens as voltage falls.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：加速電壓越高穿透力越強，所以總是對樣品更溫和。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher accelerating voltage penetrates better and is therefore always gentler on the specimen. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樣品厚度、非彈性散射與輻射損傷」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Specimen thickness, inelastic scattering and radiation damage\" is correct?","options":["高解析成像要求樣品厚度在 10 到 50 nm，電子在樣品內的非彈性平均自由徑約 100 nm 等級，厚度與自由徑之比 t/λ 可由能量損失譜的零損失峰與總強度之比求得，是每張影像都應記錄的參數。","加速電壓越高穿透力越強，所以總是對樣品更溫和。","顯微鏡放在地下室就自動滿足振動與磁場規格。"],"optionsEn":["High-resolution imaging needs specimens 10 to 50 nm thick.","Higher accelerating voltage penetrates better and is therefore always gentler on the specimen.","Putting the microscope in a basement automatically satisfies vibration and field specifications."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高解析成像要求樣品厚度在 10 到 50 nm，電子在樣品內的非彈性平均自由徑約 100 nm 等級，厚度與自由徑之比 t/λ 可由能量損失譜的零損失峰與總強度之比求得，是每張影像都應記錄的參數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"High-resolution imaging needs specimens 10 to 50 nm thick; the inelastic mean free path is of order 100 nm, and the ratio t/λ, obtained from the zero-loss to total intensity ratio in an energy-loss spectrum, is a parameter that should be recorded with every image. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"a442-v12-22","title":"樣品厚度、非彈性散射與輻射損傷：定量估算","titleEn":"Specimen thickness, inelastic scattering and radiation damage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樣品厚度、劑量與撞擊損傷」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Specimen thickness, dose and knock-on damage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：最大傳遞能量 E_max = 2E(E + 2m₀c²)/(Mc²)。碳（M = 12 u）：300 kV 為 71 eV、200 kV 為 44 eV、80 kV 為 15.8 eV；石墨烯的位移閾值約 17 到 20 eV，所以 80 kV 以下才安全。矽 300 kV 為 30 eV、金只有 4.3 eV。厚度：t/λ = 0.5（t ≈ 50 nm）時未散射比例 exp(−0.5) = 61%，t/λ = 0.2 時 82%，晶格影像的可解讀性隨 t/λ 迅速下降。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Maximum transferred energy E_max = 2E(E + 2m₀c²)/(Mc²). For carbon (M = 12 u): 71 eV at 300 kV, 44 eV at 200 kV, 15.8 eV at 80 kV; graphene's displacement threshold is about 17 to 20 eV, so only 80 kV and below is safe. Silicon at 300 kV gets 30 eV and gold only 4.3 eV. Thickness: at t/λ = 0.5 (t ≈ 50 nm) the unscattered fraction is exp(−0.5) = 61%, at t/λ = 0.2 it is 82%, and lattice-image interpretability falls quickly with t/λ. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：每個分析區域先量 EELS 的 t/λ 並記錄；對損傷敏感的樣品在固定區域以固定劑量率連續拍攝，量繞射點強度或晶格條紋對比隨累積劑量衰減的曲線，決定臨界劑量；在 300、200、80 kV 重複，確認撞擊型損傷隨電壓降低而減輕、電離型損傷則相反。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure and record EELS t/λ for every analysis region; on damage-sensitive specimens record continuously on one area at a fixed dose rate, plot the decay of diffraction-spot intensity or lattice-fringe contrast against accumulated dose to find the critical dose; repeat at 300, 200 and 80 kV and confirm that knock-on damage eases as voltage falls while radiolysis does the opposite.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"最大傳遞能量 E_max = 2E(E + 2m₀c²)/(Mc²)。碳（M = 12 u）：300 kV 為 71 eV、200 kV 為 44 eV、80 kV 為 15.8 eV；石墨烯的位移閾值約 17 到 20 eV，所以 80 kV 以下才安全。矽 300 kV 為 30 eV、金只有 4.3 eV。厚度：t/λ = 0.5（t ≈ 50 nm）時未散射比例 exp(−0.5) = 61%，t/λ = 0.2 時 82%，晶格影像的可解讀性隨 t/λ 迅速下降。","textEn":"Maximum transferred energy E_max = 2E(E + 2m₀c²)/(Mc²). For carbon (M = 12 u): 71 eV at 300 kV, 44 eV at 200 kV, 15.8 eV at 80 kV; graphene's displacement threshold is about 17 to 20 eV, so only 80 kV and below is safe. Silicon at 300 kV gets 30 eV and gold only 4.3 eV. Thickness: at t/λ = 0.5 (t ≈ 50 nm) the unscattered fraction is exp(−0.5) = 61%, at t/λ = 0.2 it is 82%, and lattice-image interpretability falls quickly with t/λ.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樣品厚度、非彈性散射與輻射損傷」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Specimen thickness, inelastic scattering and radiation damage\", which statement holds?","options":["穿透電子顯微鏡的影像對比和光學顯微鏡一樣來自吸收。","最大傳遞能量 E_max = 2E(E + 2m₀c²)/(Mc²)。","只要像差校正器調好，電子槍的能量散佈就無關緊要。"],"optionsEn":["TEM image contrast comes from absorption, as in a light microscope.","Maximum transferred energy E_max = 2E(E + 2m₀c²)/(Mc²).","Once the corrector is tuned, the gun's energy spread no longer matters."],"answer":1,"explanation":"最大傳遞能量 E_max = 2E(E + 2m₀c²)/(Mc²)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Maximum transferred energy E_max = 2E(E + 2m₀c²)/(Mc²). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"a442-v12-23","title":"樣品厚度、非彈性散射與輻射損傷：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Specimen thickness, inelastic scattering and radiation damage: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「樣品厚度、劑量與撞擊損傷」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Specimen thickness, dose and knock-on damage” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"每個分析區域先量 EELS 的 t/λ 並記錄；對損傷敏感的樣品在固定區域以固定劑量率連續拍攝，量繞射點強度或晶格條紋對比隨累積劑量衰減的曲線，決定臨界劑量；在 300、200、80 kV 重複，確認撞擊型損傷隨電壓降低而減輕、電離型損傷則相反。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure and record EELS t/λ for every analysis region; on damage-sensitive specimens record continuously on one area at a fixed dose rate, plot the decay of diffraction-spot intensity or lattice-fringe contrast against accumulated dose to find the critical dose; repeat at 300, 200 and 80 kV and confirm that knock-on damage eases as voltage falls while radiolysis does the opposite. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：在 300 kV 觀察二維材料，幾秒內晶格出現空位並擴成孔洞，分析者把孔洞當成材料固有缺陷並發表缺陷密度；改用 80 kV 重做時缺陷消失。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Observing a two-dimensional material at 300 kV creates vacancies within seconds that grow into holes; the analyst reports the holes as intrinsic defects and publishes a defect density, and the defects vanish when the work is repeated at 80 kV.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每個分析區域先量 EELS 的 t/λ 並記錄；對損傷敏感的樣品在固定區域以固定劑量率連續拍攝，量繞射點強度或晶格條紋對比隨累積劑量衰減的曲線，決定臨界劑量；在 300、200、80 kV 重複，確認撞擊型損傷隨電壓降低而減輕、電離型損傷則相反。","textEn":"Measure and record EELS t/λ for every analysis region; on damage-sensitive specimens record continuously on one area at a fixed dose rate, plot the decay of diffraction-spot intensity or lattice-fringe contrast against accumulated dose to find the critical dose; repeat at 300, 200 and 80 kV and confirm that knock-on damage eases as voltage falls while radiolysis does the opposite.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-23-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樣品厚度、非彈性散射與輻射損傷」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Specimen thickness, inelastic scattering and radiation damage\"?","options":["只要模擬結果看起來合理，就可以省略實體量測與校正。","極靴間隙越小越好，因為像差係數更低。","每個分析區域先量 EELS 的 t/λ 並記錄。"],"optionsEn":["If the simulation looks reasonable, physical measurement and calibration can be skipped.","A smaller pole-piece gap is always better because aberration coefficients are lower.","Measure and record EELS t/λ for every analysis region."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每個分析區域先量 EELS 的 t/λ 並記錄；對損傷敏感的樣品在固定區域以固定劑量率連續拍攝，量繞射點強度或晶格條紋對比隨累積劑量衰減的曲線，決定臨界劑量；在 300、200、80 kV 重複，確認撞擊型損傷隨電壓降低而減輕、電離型損傷則相反。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure and record EELS t/λ for every analysis region; on damage-sensitive specimens record continuously on one area at a fixed dose rate, plot the decay of diffraction-spot intensity or lattice-fringe contrast against accumulated dose to find the critical dose; repeat at 300, 200 and 80 kV and confirm that knock-on damage eases as voltage falls while radiolysis does the opposite. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"a442-v12-24","title":"樣品厚度、非彈性散射與輻射損傷：失效診斷","titleEn":"Specimen thickness, inelastic scattering and radiation damage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樣品厚度、劑量與撞擊損傷」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Specimen thickness, dose and knock-on damage” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"在 300 kV 觀察二維材料，幾秒內晶格出現空位並擴成孔洞，分析者把孔洞當成材料固有缺陷並發表缺陷密度；改用 80 kV 重做時缺陷消失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Observing a two-dimensional material at 300 kV creates vacancies within seconds that grow into holes; the analyst reports the holes as intrinsic defects and publishes a defect density, and the defects vanish when the work is repeated at 80 kV. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：因此加速電壓是依樣品而選的參數，不是越高越好。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Accelerating voltage is therefore chosen per specimen, not simply maximised.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「加速電壓越高穿透力越強，所以總是對樣品更溫和。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher accelerating voltage penetrates better and is therefore always gentler on the specimen.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在 300 kV 觀察二維材料，幾秒內晶格出現空位並擴成孔洞，分析者把孔洞當成材料固有缺陷並發表缺陷密度；改用 80 kV 重做時缺陷消失。","textEn":"Observing a two-dimensional material at 300 kV creates vacancies within seconds that grow into holes; the analyst reports the holes as intrinsic defects and publishes a defect density, and the defects vanish when the work is repeated at 80 kV.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樣品厚度、非彈性散射與輻射損傷」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Specimen thickness, inelastic scattering and radiation damage\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["在 300 kV 觀察二維材料，幾秒內晶格出現空位並擴成孔洞，分析者把孔洞當成材料固有缺陷並發表缺陷密度；改用 80 kV 重做時缺陷消失。","只要重新開機或重設軟體，硬體失效也會一併排除。","顯微鏡放在地下室就自動滿足振動與磁場規格。"],"optionsEn":["Observing a two-dimensional material at 300 kV creates vacancies within seconds that grow into holes.","Restarting or resetting the software also clears hardware failures.","Putting the microscope in a basement automatically satisfies vibration and field specifications."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在 300 kV 觀察二維材料，幾秒內晶格出現空位並擴成孔洞，分析者把孔洞當成材料固有缺陷並發表缺陷密度；改用 80 kV 重做時缺陷消失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Observing a two-dimensional material at 300 kV creates vacancies within seconds that grow into holes; the analyst reports the holes as intrinsic defects and publishes a defect density, and the defects vanish when the work is repeated at 80 kV. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"a442-v12-s4","title":"系統整合、驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Integration, validation and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「場址環境：磁場、溫度、振動與聲學」與「解析度驗收、穩定度驗證與工程交接」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Site environment: magnetic fields, temperature, vibration and acoustics\" and \"Resolution acceptance, stability validation and engineering handoff\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a442-v12-25","title":"場址環境：磁場、溫度、振動與聲學：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Site environment: magnetic fields, temperature, vibration and acoustics: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-24"],"objective":"說明「鏡筒外罩、磁場消除與溫控」如何決定穿透電子顯微鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Column enclosure, field cancellation and temperature control” determines the key performance of “Transmission electron microscopes”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"像差校正顯微鏡的解析度與穩定度綁在一起，場址必須把干擾壓到影像週期的十分之一以下：交流雜散磁場偏轉電子束並以電源頻率抖動影像；室溫漂移改變透鏡線圈電阻與鏡筒長度，使焦點與放大率緩慢漂移；地板振動與聲壓直接搖動樣品相對於物鏡的位置。對策包含鏡筒外的磁屏蔽與主動磁場消除、±0.1 °C 的房間溫控與鏡筒水冷恆溫、主動隔振基座與隔音外罩，以及把電子設備與操作者移到隔壁房間以遠端操作。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「鏡筒外罩、磁場消除與溫控」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Aberration-corrected microscopes tie resolution to stability, and the site must hold disturbances below a tenth of the image period: ac stray fields deflect the beam and jitter the image at mains frequency; room-temperature drift changes lens-coil resistance and column length so focus and magnification creep; floor vibration and sound pressure shake the specimen relative to the objective. Countermeasures include magnetic shielding and active field cancellation around the column, ±0.1 °C room control with temperature-stabilised lens cooling water, an active isolation base, acoustic enclosures, and moving electronics and operators to an adjacent room for remote operation. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Column enclosure, field cancellation and temperature control”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：磁場偏轉：300 kV 電子動量 p = 3.37×10⁻²² kg·m/s，B = 10 nT（0.1 mG）時迴轉半徑 r = p/(eB) ≈ 2.1×10⁵ m；在物鏡附近 50 mm 未屏蔽路徑上橫移 ≈ L²/(2r) ≈ 6 nm，鐵質極靴與屏蔽提供約 100 倍衰減後為 0.06 nm，恰在 0.1 nm 解析度的容許邊緣，所以常見場址規格是 0.1 mG 等級。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Field deflection: a 300 kV electron has momentum p = 3.37×10⁻²² kg·m/s, so at B = 10 nT (0.1 mG) the gyration radius is r = p/(eB) ≈ 2.1×10⁵ m; over an unshielded 50 mm path near the objective the lateral shift is ≈ L²/(2r) ≈ 6 nm, and about 100-fold attenuation by iron pole pieces and shielding leaves 0.06 nm, right at the tolerance edge for 0.1 nm resolution, which is why 0.1 mG-class site specifications are common.","failure":"常見誤解：「顯微鏡放在地下室就自動滿足振動與磁場規格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Putting the microscope in a basement automatically satisfies vibration and field specifications.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「鏡筒外罩、磁場消除與溫控」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Column enclosure, field cancellation and temperature control”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-25-k1","title":"場址環境：磁場、溫度、振動與聲學","titleEn":"Site environment: magnetic fields, temperature, vibration and acoustics","text":"像差校正顯微鏡的解析度與穩定度綁在一起，場址必須把干擾壓到影像週期的十分之一以下：交流雜散磁場偏轉電子束並以電源頻率抖動影像；室溫漂移改變透鏡線圈電阻與鏡筒長度，使焦點與放大率緩慢漂移；地板振動與聲壓直接搖動樣品相對於物鏡的位置。對策包含鏡筒外的磁屏蔽與主動磁場消除、±0.1 °C 的房間溫控與鏡筒水冷恆溫、主動隔振基座與隔音外罩，以及把電子設備與操作者移到隔壁房間以遠端操作。","textEn":"Aberration-corrected microscopes tie resolution to stability, and the site must hold disturbances below a tenth of the image period: ac stray fields deflect the beam and jitter the image at mains frequency; room-temperature drift changes lens-coil resistance and column length so focus and magnification creep; floor vibration and sound pressure shake the specimen relative to the objective. Countermeasures include magnetic shielding and active field cancellation around the column, ±0.1 °C room control with temperature-stabilised lens cooling water, an active isolation base, acoustic enclosures, and moving electronics and operators to an adjacent room for remote operation.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：顯微鏡放在地下室就自動滿足振動與磁場規格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Putting the microscope in a basement automatically satisfies vibration and field specifications. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「場址環境：磁場、溫度、振動與聲學」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Site environment: magnetic fields, temperature, vibration and acoustics\" is correct?","options":["顯微鏡放在地下室就自動滿足振動與磁場規格。","像差校正顯微鏡的解析度與穩定度綁在一起，場址必須把干擾壓到影像週期的十分之一以下：交流雜散磁場偏轉電子束並以電源頻率抖動影像。","規格表上的解析度就是日常使用時可達到的解析度。"],"optionsEn":["Putting the microscope in a basement automatically satisfies vibration and field specifications.","Aberration-corrected microscopes tie resolution to stability, and the site must hold disturbances below a tenth of the image period: ac stray fields deflect the beam and jitter the image at mains frequency.","The resolution on the specification sheet is the resolution achieved in daily use."],"answer":1,"explanation":"像差校正顯微鏡的解析度與穩定度綁在一起，場址必須把干擾壓到影像週期的十分之一以下：交流雜散磁場偏轉電子束並以電源頻率抖動影像；室溫漂移改變透鏡線圈電阻與鏡筒長度，使焦點與放大率緩慢漂移；地板振動與聲壓直接搖動樣品相對於物鏡的位置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Aberration-corrected microscopes tie resolution to stability, and the site must hold disturbances below a tenth of the image period: ac stray fields deflect the beam and jitter the image at mains frequency; room-temperature drift changes lens-coil resistance and column length so focus and magnification creep; floor vibration and sound pressure shake the specimen relative to the objective. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"a442-v12-26","title":"場址環境：磁場、溫度、振動與聲學：定量估算","titleEn":"Site environment: magnetic fields, temperature, vibration and acoustics: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鏡筒外罩、磁場消除與溫控」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Column enclosure, field cancellation and temperature control” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：磁場偏轉：300 kV 電子動量 p = 3.37×10⁻²² kg·m/s，B = 10 nT（0.1 mG）時迴轉半徑 r = p/(eB) ≈ 2.1×10⁵ m；在物鏡附近 50 mm 未屏蔽路徑上橫移 ≈ L²/(2r) ≈ 6 nm，鐵質極靴與屏蔽提供約 100 倍衰減後為 0.06 nm，恰在 0.1 nm 解析度的容許邊緣，所以常見場址規格是 0.1 mG 等級。溫度：銅線圈電阻溫度係數 0.4%/K，恆流源可補償電阻變化，但鏡筒 1 m 長的鋼體在 0.1 K 下伸長 1.2 µm，需靠溫控與熱平衡時間消化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Field deflection: a 300 kV electron has momentum p = 3.37×10⁻²² kg·m/s, so at B = 10 nT (0.1 mG) the gyration radius is r = p/(eB) ≈ 2.1×10⁵ m; over an unshielded 50 mm path near the objective the lateral shift is ≈ L²/(2r) ≈ 6 nm, and about 100-fold attenuation by iron pole pieces and shielding leaves 0.06 nm, right at the tolerance edge for 0.1 nm resolution, which is why 0.1 mG-class site specifications are common. Temperature: a copper coil's resistance coefficient of 0.4%/K is handled by constant-current supplies, but a 1 m steel column lengthens 1.2 µm per 0.1 K and must be absorbed by control and settling time. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：安裝前以磁通閘、加速規與聲壓計做 24 小時場址紀錄，與原廠規格逐項比對；安裝後在最高放大率拍 60 秒影像序列並做頻譜分析，辨認 50/60 Hz（磁場）、1 到 20 Hz（振動）與數百 Hz（聲學）各自的貢獻；開關空調、電梯與鄰近設備重複測試，建立禁用時段表。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before installation log 24 hours of field, vibration and sound with a fluxgate, accelerometer and sound-level meter and compare item by item with the vendor specification; after installation record 60 s image series at maximum magnification and spectrally separate the 50/60 Hz (field), 1 to 20 Hz (vibration) and few-hundred-hertz (acoustic) contributions; repeat while switching air handlers, lifts and neighbouring equipment to build an exclusion timetable.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"磁場偏轉：300 kV 電子動量 p = 3.37×10⁻²² kg·m/s，B = 10 nT（0.1 mG）時迴轉半徑 r = p/(eB) ≈ 2.1×10⁵ m；在物鏡附近 50 mm 未屏蔽路徑上橫移 ≈ L²/(2r) ≈ 6 nm，鐵質極靴與屏蔽提供約 100 倍衰減後為 0.06 nm，恰在 0.1 nm 解析度的容許邊緣，所以常見場址規格是 0.1 mG 等級。溫度：銅線圈電阻溫度係數 0.4%/K，恆流源可補償電阻變化，但鏡筒 1 m 長的鋼體在 0.1 K 下伸長 1.2 µm，需靠溫控與熱平衡時間消化。","textEn":"Field deflection: a 300 kV electron has momentum p = 3.37×10⁻²² kg·m/s, so at B = 10 nT (0.1 mG) the gyration radius is r = p/(eB) ≈ 2.1×10⁵ m; over an unshielded 50 mm path near the objective the lateral shift is ≈ L²/(2r) ≈ 6 nm, and about 100-fold attenuation by iron pole pieces and shielding leaves 0.06 nm, right at the tolerance edge for 0.1 nm resolution, which is why 0.1 mG-class site specifications are common. Temperature: a copper coil's resistance coefficient of 0.4%/K is handled by constant-current supplies, but a 1 m steel column lengthens 1.2 µm per 0.1 K and must be absorbed by control and settling time.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「場址環境：磁場、溫度、振動與聲學」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Site environment: magnetic fields, temperature, vibration and acoustics\", which statement holds?","options":["Cs 校正後解析度只受電子波長限制，可以達到皮米。","極靴間隙越小越好，因為像差係數更低。","磁場偏轉：300 kV 電子動量 p = 3.37×10⁻²² kg·m/s，B = 10 nT（0.1 mG）時迴轉半徑 r = p/(eB) ≈ 2.1×10⁵ m。"],"optionsEn":["After Cs correction resolution is limited only by electron wavelength and reaches picometres.","A smaller pole-piece gap is always better because aberration coefficients are lower.","Field deflection: a 300 kV electron has momentum p = 3.37×10⁻²² kg·m/s, so at B = 10 nT (0.1 mG) the gyration radius is r = p/(eB) ≈ 2.1×10⁵ m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"磁場偏轉：300 kV 電子動量 p = 3.37×10⁻²² kg·m/s，B = 10 nT（0.1 mG）時迴轉半徑 r = p/(eB) ≈ 2.1×10⁵ m；在物鏡附近 50 mm 未屏蔽路徑上橫移 ≈ L²/(2r) ≈ 6 nm，鐵質極靴與屏蔽提供約 100 倍衰減後為 0.06 nm，恰在 0.1 nm 解析度的容許邊緣，所以常見場址規格是 0.1 mG 等級。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Field deflection: a 300 kV electron has momentum p = 3.37×10⁻²² kg·m/s, so at B = 10 nT (0.1 mG) the gyration radius is r = p/(eB) ≈ 2.1×10⁵ m; over an unshielded 50 mm path near the objective the lateral shift is ≈ L²/(2r) ≈ 6 nm, and about 100-fold attenuation by iron pole pieces and shielding leaves 0.06 nm, right at the tolerance edge for 0.1 nm resolution, which is why 0.1 mG-class site specifications are common. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"a442-v12-27","title":"場址環境：磁場、溫度、振動與聲學：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Site environment: magnetic fields, temperature, vibration and acoustics: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「鏡筒外罩、磁場消除與溫控」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Column enclosure, field cancellation and temperature control” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"安裝前以磁通閘、加速規與聲壓計做 24 小時場址紀錄，與原廠規格逐項比對；安裝後在最高放大率拍 60 秒影像序列並做頻譜分析，辨認 50/60 Hz（磁場）、1 到 20 Hz（振動）與數百 Hz（聲學）各自的貢獻；開關空調、電梯與鄰近設備重複測試，建立禁用時段表。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before installation log 24 hours of field, vibration and sound with a fluxgate, accelerometer and sound-level meter and compare item by item with the vendor specification; after installation record 60 s image series at maximum magnification and spectrally separate the 50/60 Hz (field), 1 to 20 Hz (vibration) and few-hundred-hertz (acoustic) contributions; repeat while switching air handlers, lifts and neighbouring equipment to build an exclusion timetable. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：新裝的隔壁核磁共振磁鐵在鏡筒位置留下 2 mG 的直流場梯度，影像沒有抖動卻出現固定的像散與對準偏移，每次換樣品都要重調；問題持續數月，直到磁場調查才發現來源在牆的另一邊。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A newly installed NMR magnet next door leaves a 2 mG dc field gradient at the column; the image does not jitter but shows fixed astigmatism and alignment offsets that must be retuned after every specimen change, and the cause stays hidden for months until a field survey finds it on the other side of the wall.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"安裝前以磁通閘、加速規與聲壓計做 24 小時場址紀錄，與原廠規格逐項比對；安裝後在最高放大率拍 60 秒影像序列並做頻譜分析，辨認 50/60 Hz（磁場）、1 到 20 Hz（振動）與數百 Hz（聲學）各自的貢獻；開關空調、電梯與鄰近設備重複測試，建立禁用時段表。","textEn":"Before installation log 24 hours of field, vibration and sound with a fluxgate, accelerometer and sound-level meter and compare item by item with the vendor specification; after installation record 60 s image series at maximum magnification and spectrally separate the 50/60 Hz (field), 1 to 20 Hz (vibration) and few-hundred-hertz (acoustic) contributions; repeat while switching air handlers, lifts and neighbouring equipment to build an exclusion timetable.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-27-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「場址環境：磁場、溫度、振動與聲學」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Site environment: magnetic fields, temperature, vibration and acoustics\"?","options":["安裝前以磁通閘、加速規與聲壓計做 24 小時場址紀錄，與原廠規格逐項比對。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","軟體顯示的比例尺是絕對的，不需要用晶格校正。"],"optionsEn":["Before installation log 24 hours of field, vibration and sound with a fluxgate, accelerometer and sound-level meter and compare item by item with the vendor specification.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The scale bar shown by the software is absolute and needs no lattice calibration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"安裝前以磁通閘、加速規與聲壓計做 24 小時場址紀錄，與原廠規格逐項比對；安裝後在最高放大率拍 60 秒影像序列並做頻譜分析，辨認 50/60 Hz（磁場）、1 到 20 Hz（振動）與數百 Hz（聲學）各自的貢獻；開關空調、電梯與鄰近設備重複測試，建立禁用時段表。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before installation log 24 hours of field, vibration and sound with a fluxgate, accelerometer and sound-level meter and compare item by item with the vendor specification; after installation record 60 s image series at maximum magnification and spectrally separate the 50/60 Hz (field), 1 to 20 Hz (vibration) and few-hundred-hertz (acoustic) contributions; repeat while switching air handlers, lifts and neighbouring equipment to build an exclusion timetable. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"a442-v12-28","title":"場址環境：磁場、溫度、振動與聲學：失效診斷","titleEn":"Site environment: magnetic fields, temperature, vibration and acoustics: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鏡筒外罩、磁場消除與溫控」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Column enclosure, field cancellation and temperature control” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"新裝的隔壁核磁共振磁鐵在鏡筒位置留下 2 mG 的直流場梯度，影像沒有抖動卻出現固定的像散與對準偏移，每次換樣品都要重調；問題持續數月，直到磁場調查才發現來源在牆的另一邊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A newly installed NMR magnet next door leaves a 2 mG dc field gradient at the column; the image does not jitter but shows fixed astigmatism and alignment offsets that must be retuned after every specimen change, and the cause stays hidden for months until a field survey finds it on the other side of the wall. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：對策包含鏡筒外的磁屏蔽與主動磁場消除、±0.1 °C 的房間溫控與鏡筒水冷恆溫、主動隔振基座與隔音外罩，以及把電子設備與操作者移到隔壁房間以遠端操作。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Countermeasures include magnetic shielding and active field cancellation around the column, ±0.1 °C room control with temperature-stabilised lens cooling water, an active isolation base, acoustic enclosures, and moving electronics and operators to an adjacent room for remote operation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「顯微鏡放在地下室就自動滿足振動與磁場規格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Putting the microscope in a basement automatically satisfies vibration and field specifications.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新裝的隔壁核磁共振磁鐵在鏡筒位置留下 2 mG 的直流場梯度，影像沒有抖動卻出現固定的像散與對準偏移，每次換樣品都要重調；問題持續數月，直到磁場調查才發現來源在牆的另一邊。","textEn":"A newly installed NMR magnet next door leaves a 2 mG dc field gradient at the column; the image does not jitter but shows fixed astigmatism and alignment offsets that must be retuned after every specimen change, and the cause stays hidden for months until a field survey finds it on the other side of the wall.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「場址環境：磁場、溫度、振動與聲學」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Site environment: magnetic fields, temperature, vibration and acoustics\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","新裝的隔壁核磁共振磁鐵在鏡筒位置留下 2 mG 的直流場梯度，影像沒有抖動卻出現固定的像散與對準偏移，每次換樣品都要重調。","規格表上的解析度就是日常使用時可達到的解析度。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","A newly installed NMR magnet next door leaves a 2 mG dc field gradient at the column.","The resolution on the specification sheet is the resolution achieved in daily use."],"answer":1,"explanation":"新裝的隔壁核磁共振磁鐵在鏡筒位置留下 2 mG 的直流場梯度，影像沒有抖動卻出現固定的像散與對準偏移，每次換樣品都要重調；問題持續數月，直到磁場調查才發現來源在牆的另一邊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A newly installed NMR magnet next door leaves a 2 mG dc field gradient at the column; the image does not jitter but shows fixed astigmatism and alignment offsets that must be retuned after every specimen change, and the cause stays hidden for months until a field survey finds it on the other side of the wall. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"a442-v12-29","title":"解析度驗收、穩定度驗證與工程交接：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Resolution acceptance, stability validation and engineering handoff: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-28"],"objective":"說明「Young 條紋、啞鈴影像與驗收清單」如何決定穿透電子顯微鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Young's fringes, dumbbell images and acceptance checklist” determines the key performance of “Transmission electron microscopes”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"驗收必須用可重複的客觀指標：資訊極限以非晶材料的 Young 條紋量到的最高空間頻率表示；點解析度以矽 [110] 的 0.136 nm 啞鈴是否分開、或以 STEM-HAADF 影像中原子柱的傅立葉峰表示；穩定度以校正後的像差表在 30 分鐘內保持在容限內、以及高壓與透鏡電流的紀錄表示。EELS 與 EDS 另有能量解析度與偵測效率的驗收項。交接文件包含每個高壓與極靴組合的校正表、像差校正程序、場址環境紀錄、樣品損傷指引與每週的穩定度例行檢查，讓後續使用者能判斷儀器是否仍在驗收狀態。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「Young 條紋、啞鈴影像與驗收清單」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Acceptance uses repeatable objective indicators: the information limit as the highest spatial frequency in Young's fringes on amorphous material; point resolution as whether the 0.136 nm silicon [110] dumbbells separate, or as Fourier peaks of atomic columns in STEM-HAADF images; stability as the corrected aberration table staying within tolerance for 30 minutes together with high-voltage and lens-current logs. EELS and EDS add energy-resolution and detection-efficiency items. The handoff package contains calibration tables for every high-voltage and pole-piece combination, the aberration-correction procedure, site environment records, specimen-damage guidance and a weekly stability routine, so later users can judge whether the instrument is still in its accepted state. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Young's fringes, dumbbell images and acceptance checklist”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：驗收門檻範例（300 kV、Cs 校正）：Young 條紋資訊極限 ≤ 0.08 nm；矽 [110] 啞鈴 0.136 nm 在 HRTEM 與 HAADF 中皆可分辨，傅立葉峰訊噪比 ≥ 3；校正後 30 分鐘內 C_s 殘餘 |C₃| ≤ 2 µm、A2 ≤ 50 nm、B2 ≤ 50 nm；高壓穩定度 ≤ 1 ppm/min；載台插入 15 分鐘後漂移 ≤ 0.5 nm/min；EELS 零損失峰半高寬 ≤ 0.8 eV（Schottky）或 ≤ 0.2 eV（單色器）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Example acceptance thresholds (300 kV, Cs corrected): Young's-fringe information limit ≤ 0.08 nm; silicon [110] dumbbells at 0.136 nm resolved in both HRTEM and HAADF with Fourier-peak signal-to-noise ≥ 3; within 30 minutes after correction residual |C₃| ≤ 2 µm, A2 ≤ 50 nm and B2 ≤ 50 nm; high-voltage stability ≤ 1 ppm/min; holder drift ≤ 0.5 nm/min 15 minutes after insertion; EELS zero-loss width ≤ 0.8 eV (Schottky) or ≤ 0.2 eV (monochromated).","failure":"常見誤解：「規格表上的解析度就是日常使用時可達到的解析度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The resolution on the specification sheet is the resolution achieved in daily use.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「Young 條紋、啞鈴影像與驗收清單」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Young's fringes, dumbbell images and acceptance checklist”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-29-k1","title":"解析度驗收、穩定度驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Resolution acceptance, stability validation and engineering handoff","text":"驗收必須用可重複的客觀指標：資訊極限以非晶材料的 Young 條紋量到的最高空間頻率表示；點解析度以矽 [110] 的 0.136 nm 啞鈴是否分開、或以 STEM-HAADF 影像中原子柱的傅立葉峰表示；穩定度以校正後的像差表在 30 分鐘內保持在容限內、以及高壓與透鏡電流的紀錄表示。EELS 與 EDS 另有能量解析度與偵測效率的驗收項。","textEn":"Acceptance uses repeatable objective indicators: the information limit as the highest spatial frequency in Young's fringes on amorphous material; point resolution as whether the 0.136 nm silicon [110] dumbbells separate, or as Fourier peaks of atomic columns in STEM-HAADF images; stability as the corrected aberration table staying within tolerance for 30 minutes together with high-voltage and lens-current logs. EELS and EDS add energy-resolution and detection-efficiency items.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：規格表上的解析度就是日常使用時可達到的解析度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The resolution on the specification sheet is the resolution achieved in daily use. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「解析度驗收、穩定度驗證與工程交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Resolution acceptance, stability validation and engineering handoff\" is correct?","options":["規格表上的解析度就是日常使用時可達到的解析度。","穿透電子顯微鏡的影像對比和光學顯微鏡一樣來自吸收。","驗收必須用可重複的客觀指標：資訊極限以非晶材料的 Young 條紋量到的最高空間頻率表示。"],"optionsEn":["The resolution on the specification sheet is the resolution achieved in daily use.","TEM image contrast comes from absorption, as in a light microscope.","Acceptance uses repeatable objective indicators: the information limit as the highest spatial frequency in Young's fringes on amorphous material."],"answer":2,"explanation":"驗收必須用可重複的客觀指標：資訊極限以非晶材料的 Young 條紋量到的最高空間頻率表示；點解析度以矽 [110] 的 0.136 nm 啞鈴是否分開、或以 STEM-HAADF 影像中原子柱的傅立葉峰表示；穩定度以校正後的像差表在 30 分鐘內保持在容限內、以及高壓與透鏡電流的紀錄表示。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Acceptance uses repeatable objective indicators: the information limit as the highest spatial frequency in Young's fringes on amorphous material; point resolution as whether the 0.136 nm silicon [110] dumbbells separate, or as Fourier peaks of atomic columns in STEM-HAADF images; stability as the corrected aberration table staying within tolerance for 30 minutes together with high-voltage and lens-current logs. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"a442-v12-30","title":"解析度驗收、穩定度驗證與工程交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Resolution acceptance, stability validation and engineering handoff: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「Young 條紋、啞鈴影像與驗收清單」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Young's fringes, dumbbell images and acceptance checklist” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：驗收門檻範例（300 kV、Cs 校正）：Young 條紋資訊極限 ≤ 0.08 nm；矽 [110] 啞鈴 0.136 nm 在 HRTEM 與 HAADF 中皆可分辨，傅立葉峰訊噪比 ≥ 3；校正後 30 分鐘內 C_s 殘餘 |C₃| ≤ 2 µm、A2 ≤ 50 nm、B2 ≤ 50 nm；高壓穩定度 ≤ 1 ppm/min；載台插入 15 分鐘後漂移 ≤ 0.5 nm/min；EELS 零損失峰半高寬 ≤ 0.8 eV（Schottky）或 ≤ 0.2 eV（單色器）。任一項未達即不簽收。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Example acceptance thresholds (300 kV, Cs corrected): Young's-fringe information limit ≤ 0.08 nm; silicon [110] dumbbells at 0.136 nm resolved in both HRTEM and HAADF with Fourier-peak signal-to-noise ≥ 3; within 30 minutes after correction residual |C₃| ≤ 2 µm, A2 ≤ 50 nm and B2 ≤ 50 nm; high-voltage stability ≤ 1 ppm/min; holder drift ≤ 0.5 nm/min 15 minutes after insertion; EELS zero-loss width ≤ 0.8 eV (Schottky) or ≤ 0.2 eV (monochromated). Any failed item blocks sign-off. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：依清單在同一天內由原廠與使用方共同執行每項測試，所有原始影像、傅立葉轉換、像差表與電源紀錄存檔並附時間戳；一週後由使用方獨立重測資訊極限與漂移，確認結果在驗收值的 10% 內，作為日後退化判斷的基線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run every listed test jointly by vendor and user within one day, archive all raw images, Fourier transforms, aberration tables and supply logs with time stamps; one week later the user independently repeats the information-limit and drift tests and confirms results within 10% of the acceptance values, establishing the baseline for later degradation judgements.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"驗收門檻範例（300 kV、Cs 校正）：Young 條紋資訊極限 ≤ 0.08 nm；矽 [110] 啞鈴 0.136 nm 在 HRTEM 與 HAADF 中皆可分辨，傅立葉峰訊噪比 ≥ 3；校正後 30 分鐘內 C_s 殘餘 |C₃| ≤ 2 µm、A2 ≤ 50 nm、B2 ≤ 50 nm；高壓穩定度 ≤ 1 ppm/min；載台插入 15 分鐘後漂移 ≤ 0.5 nm/min；EELS 零損失峰半高寬 ≤ 0.8 eV（Schottky）或 ≤ 0.2 eV（單色器）。任一項未達即不簽收。","textEn":"Example acceptance thresholds (300 kV, Cs corrected): Young's-fringe information limit ≤ 0.08 nm; silicon [110] dumbbells at 0.136 nm resolved in both HRTEM and HAADF with Fourier-peak signal-to-noise ≥ 3; within 30 minutes after correction residual |C₃| ≤ 2 µm, A2 ≤ 50 nm and B2 ≤ 50 nm; high-voltage stability ≤ 1 ppm/min; holder drift ≤ 0.5 nm/min 15 minutes after insertion; EELS zero-loss width ≤ 0.8 eV (Schottky) or ≤ 0.2 eV (monochromated). Any failed item blocks sign-off.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「解析度驗收、穩定度驗證與工程交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Resolution acceptance, stability validation and engineering handoff\", which statement holds?","options":["驗收門檻範例（300 kV、Cs 校正）：Young 條紋資訊極限 ≤ 0.08 nm。","只要像差校正器調好，電子槍的能量散佈就無關緊要。","軟體顯示的比例尺是絕對的，不需要用晶格校正。"],"optionsEn":["Example acceptance thresholds (300 kV, Cs corrected): Young's-fringe information limit ≤ 0.08 nm.","Once the corrector is tuned, the gun's energy spread no longer matters.","The scale bar shown by the software is absolute and needs no lattice calibration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"驗收門檻範例（300 kV、Cs 校正）：Young 條紋資訊極限 ≤ 0.08 nm；矽 [110] 啞鈴 0.136 nm 在 HRTEM 與 HAADF 中皆可分辨，傅立葉峰訊噪比 ≥ 3；校正後 30 分鐘內 C_s 殘餘 |C₃| ≤ 2 µm、A2 ≤ 50 nm、B2 ≤ 50 nm；高壓穩定度 ≤ 1 ppm/min；載台插入 15 分鐘後漂移 ≤ 0.5 nm/min；EELS 零損失峰半高寬 ≤ 0.8 eV（Schottky）或 ≤ 0.2 eV（單色器）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Example acceptance thresholds (300 kV, Cs corrected): Young's-fringe information limit ≤ 0.08 nm; silicon [110] dumbbells at 0.136 nm resolved in both HRTEM and HAADF with Fourier-peak signal-to-noise ≥ 3; within 30 minutes after correction residual |C₃| ≤ 2 µm, A2 ≤ 50 nm and B2 ≤ 50 nm; high-voltage stability ≤ 1 ppm/min; holder drift ≤ 0.5 nm/min 15 minutes after insertion; EELS zero-loss width ≤ 0.8 eV (Schottky) or ≤ 0.2 eV (monochromated). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"a442-v12-31","title":"解析度驗收、穩定度驗證與工程交接：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Resolution acceptance, stability validation and engineering handoff: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「Young 條紋、啞鈴影像與驗收清單」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Young's fringes, dumbbell images and acceptance checklist” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"依清單在同一天內由原廠與使用方共同執行每項測試，所有原始影像、傅立葉轉換、像差表與電源紀錄存檔並附時間戳；一週後由使用方獨立重測資訊極限與漂移，確認結果在驗收值的 10% 內，作為日後退化判斷的基線。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run every listed test jointly by vendor and user within one day, archive all raw images, Fourier transforms, aberration tables and supply logs with time stamps; one week later the user independently repeats the information-limit and drift tests and confirms results within 10% of the acceptance values, establishing the baseline for later degradation judgements. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：驗收只在原廠工程師調機後的黃金一小時內拍到一張 0.08 nm 的 Young 條紋便簽收，沒有要求 30 分鐘穩定度；交機後使用者每次都要花兩小時重調校正器，實際可用解析度只有 0.12 nm。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Acceptance signed on a single 0.08 nm Young's-fringe image taken in the golden hour after the factory engineer's tuning, with no 30-minute stability requirement; afterwards users spend two hours re-tuning the corrector every session and the practically usable resolution is 0.12 nm.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依清單在同一天內由原廠與使用方共同執行每項測試，所有原始影像、傅立葉轉換、像差表與電源紀錄存檔並附時間戳；一週後由使用方獨立重測資訊極限與漂移，確認結果在驗收值的 10% 內，作為日後退化判斷的基線。","textEn":"Run every listed test jointly by vendor and user within one day, archive all raw images, Fourier transforms, aberration tables and supply logs with time stamps; one week later the user independently repeats the information-limit and drift tests and confirms results within 10% of the acceptance values, establishing the baseline for later degradation judgements.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-31-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「解析度驗收、穩定度驗證與工程交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Resolution acceptance, stability validation and engineering handoff\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","依清單在同一天內由原廠與使用方共同執行每項測試，所有原始影像、傅立葉轉換、像差表與電源紀錄存檔並附時間戳。","加速電壓越高穿透力越強，所以總是對樣品更溫和。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Run every listed test jointly by vendor and user within one day, archive all raw images, Fourier transforms, aberration tables and supply logs with time stamps.","Higher accelerating voltage penetrates better and is therefore always gentler on the specimen."],"answer":1,"explanation":"依清單在同一天內由原廠與使用方共同執行每項測試，所有原始影像、傅立葉轉換、像差表與電源紀錄存檔並附時間戳；一週後由使用方獨立重測資訊極限與漂移，確認結果在驗收值的 10% 內，作為日後退化判斷的基線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run every listed test jointly by vendor and user within one day, archive all raw images, Fourier transforms, aberration tables and supply logs with time stamps; one week later the user independently repeats the information-limit and drift tests and confirms results within 10% of the acceptance values, establishing the baseline for later degradation judgements. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"a442-v12-32","title":"解析度驗收、穩定度驗證與工程交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Resolution acceptance, stability validation and engineering handoff: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"prerequisiteIds":["a442-v12-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「Young 條紋、啞鈴影像與驗收清單」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Young's fringes, dumbbell images and acceptance checklist” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"驗收只在原廠工程師調機後的黃金一小時內拍到一張 0.08 nm 的 Young 條紋便簽收，沒有要求 30 分鐘穩定度；交機後使用者每次都要花兩小時重調校正器，實際可用解析度只有 0.12 nm。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Acceptance signed on a single 0.08 nm Young's-fringe image taken in the golden hour after the factory engineer's tuning, with no 30-minute stability requirement; afterwards users spend two hours re-tuning the corrector every session and the practically usable resolution is 0.12 nm. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：交接文件包含每個高壓與極靴組合的校正表、像差校正程序、場址環境紀錄、樣品損傷指引與每週的穩定度例行檢查，讓後續使用者能判斷儀器是否仍在驗收狀態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The handoff package contains calibration tables for every high-voltage and pole-piece combination, the aberration-correction procedure, site environment records, specimen-damage guidance and a weekly stability routine, so later users can judge whether the instrument is still in its accepted state.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「規格表上的解析度就是日常使用時可達到的解析度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The resolution on the specification sheet is the resolution achieved in daily use.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a442-v12-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"驗收只在原廠工程師調機後的黃金一小時內拍到一張 0.08 nm 的 Young 條紋便簽收，沒有要求 30 分鐘穩定度；交機後使用者每次都要花兩小時重調校正器，實際可用解析度只有 0.12 nm。","textEn":"Acceptance signed on a single 0.08 nm Young's-fringe image taken in the golden hour after the factory engineer's tuning, with no 30-minute stability requirement; afterwards users spend two hours re-tuning the corrector every session and the practically usable resolution is 0.12 nm.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]},{"id":"a442-v12-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「解析度驗收、穩定度驗證與工程交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Resolution acceptance, stability validation and engineering handoff\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","穿透電子顯微鏡的影像對比和光學顯微鏡一樣來自吸收。","驗收只在原廠工程師調機後的黃金一小時內拍到一張 0.08 nm 的 Young 條紋便簽收，沒有要求 30 分鐘穩定度。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","TEM image contrast comes from absorption, as in a light microscope.","Acceptance signed on a single 0.08 nm Young's-fringe image taken in the golden hour after the factory engineer's tuning, with no 30-minute stability requirement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"驗收只在原廠工程師調機後的黃金一小時內拍到一張 0.08 nm 的 Young 條紋便簽收，沒有要求 30 分鐘穩定度；交機後使用者每次都要花兩小時重調校正器，實際可用解析度只有 0.12 nm。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Acceptance signed on a single 0.08 nm Young's-fringe image taken in the golden hour after the factory engineer's tuning, with no 30-minute stability requirement; afterwards users spend two hours re-tuning the corrector every session and the practically usable resolution is 0.12 nm. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4}],"sourceIds":["v12o-jeol-tem-products","v12o-thermofisher-tem","v12o-wikipedia-tem"],"curriculumVersion":12,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":800}};
